{"record_id":"D32-B44-R002","dataset_id":"D32","batch_id":"B44","topic":"Context-aware database queries","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","code_applicability":"CODE_HEAVY","language":"Go","language_version":"Go 1.26","objective":"Propagate cancellation and deadlines into database operations through context-aware APIs.","requirements":["Accept request-scoped context","Use QueryContext, QueryRowContext, or ExecContext where appropriate","Handle context cancellation explicitly"],"constraints":["Driver support can affect cancellation behavior","Context cancellation does not guarantee immediate database-side termination in every driver/system"],"inputs":["context.Context","SQL statement","arguments"],"outputs":["database result or context/database error"],"source_code":"func findUser(ctx context.Context, db *sql.DB, id int64) (User, error) {\n    var u User\n    err := db.QueryRowContext(ctx,\n        "SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE id = ?", id,\n    ).Scan(&u.ID, &u.Name)\n    return u, err\n}","correct_code":"Propagate the caller's context into the database API rather than replacing it with context.Background().","incorrect_code":"func findUser(ctx context.Context, db *sql.DB, id int64) (User, error) {\n    return queryUsingContext(context.Background(), db, id)\n}","failure_mode":"Caller cancellation and deadlines do not reach the database operation.","root_cause":"Request context is discarded.","testing":["Cancellation test","Deadline test","Database failure test"],"verification":"Verify that cancellation is propagated through the application layer and that returned errors are handled according to the API contract.","execution_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","validation_status":"STRUCTURALLY_VALIDATED_NOT_EXECUTED","evidence_level":"DOCUMENTED","confidence":0.98,"provenance":[{"source_locator":"go.dev/doc/database","source_type":"official_go_documentation","claim":"database/sql provides context-aware database operations."}],"relationships":[{"type":"implements","target":"D3