{"record_id":"D32-B91-R01","dataset_id":"D32","batch":"B91","topic":"io.Reader and io.Writer contract design","knowledge_type":"CONCEPT","code_applicability":"CODE_HEAVY","language":"Go","version_scope":"Current Go","objective":"Design components around Go's Reader and Writer contracts so data-processing stages remain composable.","requirements":["Handle returned byte counts correctly.","Handle EOF and other errors according to the interface contract.","Do not assume one Read or Write transfers the entire requested payload."],"constraints":["Reader and Writer implementations may legally perform partial operations.","Higher-level helpers can simplify common complete-transfer requirements."],"inputs":["byte stream"],"outputs":["consumed or produced bytes"],"expected_behavior":"Components correctly process partial reads/writes and propagate errors.","source_code":"func copyChunk(dst io.Writer, src io.Reader, buf []byte) error {\n    n, err := src.Read(buf)\n    if n > 0 {\n        written, werr := dst.Write(buf[:n])\n        if werr != nil { return werr }\n        if written != n { return io.ErrShortWrite }\n    }\n    if err != nil { return err }\n    return nil\n}","incorrect_code":"n, _ := src.Read(buf)\ndst.Write(buf[:len(buf)])","corrected_code":"n, err := src.Read(buf)\nif n > 0 { if , werr := dst.Write(buf[:n]); werr != nil { return werr } }\nif err != nil { return err }","failure_mode":"Data truncation or invalid bytes written after a partial read.","root_cause":"The implementation assumed Read fills the requested buffer and ignored the returned count.","testing":"Use readers that intentionally return short reads and injected errors.","verification":{"generated":true,"parsed":false,"executed":false,"tested":false,"passed":false,"verified":false,"requirement_satisfied":false},"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"UNVERIFIED","evidence_level":"PRIMARY_DOCUMENTATION","confidence":0.99,"provenance":["pkg.go.dev/io"],"relationships":["implements","r