{"record_id":"D35-B012-R02","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Idempotent Command Implementation","subtopic":"Request identity","concept":"An idempotency key identifies one logical command independently of transport attempts.","knowledge_type":"CONCEPT","question":"What makes an idempotency key suitable for command deduplication?","answer":"It must remain stable across retries of the same logical operation and be sufficiently scoped to avoid accidental collisions between unrelated operations.","explanation":"The key is an operation identity, not merely a timestamp or transport message identifier. Its scope and lifecycle must be defined by the command contract.","principle":"Identity must represent the logical operation being retried.","objective":"Define reliable command identity for duplicate detection.","requirements":["Stable across retries.","Unique within its declared scope.","Bound to the intended command semantics."],"constraints":["Global uniqueness is not always necessary if scope is explicit.","Key retention affects replay behavior."],"preconditions":["The command contract defines retry semantics."],"input":"Logical command identity and scope.","output":"A stable idempotency-key contract.","expected_behavior":"Equivalent retries map to the same operation identity.","incorrect_code":"key = str(time.time())","corrected_code":"key = command.idempotency_key","failure_mode":"Each retry receives a different identity and bypasses deduplication.","expected_error":"No duplicate-specific error; duplicate effect may occur.","cause":"Key is regenerated per attempt.","root_cause":"Transport attempt identity was confused with logical operation identity.","solution":"Generate or accept the idempotency key outside the retry loop and preserve it for every retry.","edge_case":"Two legitimate operations may intentionally use different keys even when their payloads are identical.","security_implication":"Keys should not be treated as authorization credentials.","performance_implication":"High-cardinality indexed keys require storage and index maintenance.","test_case":"Retry the same logical command after a simulated timeout.","test_input":"One command identity with multiple transport attempts.","expected_test_result":"All attempts resolve to one logical operation.","testing_guidance":"Separate command identity from HTTP/message delivery identifiers in tests.","verification_method":"Compare persisted command identities across attempts.","verification_guidance":"Verify that retry attempts reuse the exact key and unrelated operations do not.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":["Command contract"],"execution_requirements":["Application layer supporting explicit command identity"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.96,"related_records":["D35-B012-R01"],"depends_on":[],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":[],"tests":["D35-B012-R04"],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Established idempotency-key design practice"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B012-R03","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Idempotent Command Implementation","subtopic":"Payload consistency","concept":"An idempotency key must not silently associate different command payloads with one operation.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"How should an implementation handle the same idempotency key with a different payload?","answer":"Persist a deterministic request fingerprint or equivalent contract information and reject a key reuse that conflicts with the original request.","explanation":"Without payload consistency checking, a client could accidentally or maliciously reuse an existing key for a different command and receive an unrelated result.","principle":"Idempotency identity must be bound to the intended command semantics.","objective":"Prevent ambiguous reuse of an idempotency key.","requirements":["Persist enough information to compare relevant command fields.","Reject incompatible reuse.","Return a deterministic application-level conflict."],"constraints":["The fingerprint must exclude fields that legitimately vary between retries.","Sensitive payloads should not be stored unnecessarily."],"preconditions":["The command has a stable representation for relevant fields."],"input":"Existing idempotency record and incoming command.","output":"Original result for equivalent payload or conflict for incompatible payload.","expected_behavior":"Equivalent retry succeeds according to idempotency semantics; conflicting reuse is rejected.","incorrect_code":"if idempotency.exists(key):\n    return idempotency.result(key)","corrected_code":"existing = idempotency.get(key)\nif existing:\n    if existing.fingerprint != fingerprint(command):\n        raise IdempotencyConflict()\n    return existing.result","failure_mode":"Different commands sharing a key are incorrectly treated as the same request.","expected_error":"IdempotencyConflict or equivalent domain/application error.","cause":"Duplicate detection checks only the key.","root_cause":"The contract does not bind key identity to command payload semantics.","solution":"Store and compare a suitable request fingerprint or canonical request representation.","edge_case":"Equivalent payloads with different serialization order should produce the same canonical fingerprint.","security_implication":"Conflict detection reduces replay ambiguity but does not replace authentication or authorization.","performance_implication":"Fingerprint calculation is usually cheaper than repeating an external business operation, but canonicalization can add CPU cost for large payloads.","test_case":"Submit two different payloads with one key.","test_input":"Same key, different amount.","expected_test_result":"Second request is rejected as an idempotency conflict.","testing_guidance":"Test canonical-equivalent payloads as well as genuinely different payloads.","verification_method":"Compare stored and incoming canonical fingerprints.","verification_guidance":"Verify no second business effect is executed before conflict detection.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":["Idempotency store","Canonical request/fingerprint function"],"execution_requirements":["Persistent idempotency storage"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.95,"related_records":["D35-B012-R01","D35-B012-R02"],"depends_on":["D35-B012-R02"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":["D35-B012-R01"],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":[],"tests":["D35-B012-R04"],"verifies":["D35-B012-R05"],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Established idempotency request-consistency practice"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B012-R04","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Idempotent Command Implementation","subtopic":"Retry testing","concept":"Idempotency testing must cover repeated, conflicting, and concurrent delivery patterns.","knowledge_type":"TEST","question":"Which tests are required for an idempotent command implementation?","answer":"Test identical retries, same-key conflicting payloads, and concurrent duplicate submissions.","explanation":"A command can appear idempotent in sequential tests but fail when two requests race before either writes the idempotency record.","principle":"Retry safety must be tested under both repetition and concurrency.","objective":"Detect duplicate effects and race conditions.","requirements":["Test repeated identical commands.","Test conflicting payload reuse.","Test concurrent duplicate requests."],"constraints":["Concurrency tests need a real or representative persistence implementation.","Timing-only tests are insufficient evidence of correctness."],"preconditions":["Command has an explicit idempotency contract."],"input":"Command and repeated/concurrent delivery scenarios.","output":"Test evidence covering duplicate-effect prevention.","expected_behavior":"One logical effect per idempotency key.","incorrect_code":"assert service.run(command) == service.run(command)","corrected_code":"first = service.run(command)\nsecond = service.run(command)\nassert first == second\nassert repo.effect_count(command.idempotency_key) == 1","failure_mode":"Tests validate returned equality but not business-effect cardinality.","expected_error":"Assertion failure when duplicate side effects occur.","cause":"Test does not inspect durable business state.","root_cause":"Idempotency was defined as response equality instead of effect safety.","solution":"Assert both response semantics and durable effect count.","edge_case":"Concurrent requests can produce different intermediate results if the implementation lacks an