{"record_id":"D35-B014-R01","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"State Machine Implementation","subtopic":"Explicit state transitions","concept":"A state machine implementation represents allowed states and transitions explicitly instead of scattering transition rules across unrelated code.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"How should an architectural state machine be implemented?","answer":"Represent valid states and transition rules explicitly and expose a controlled transition operation that rejects invalid state changes.","explanation":"Explicit transition logic turns lifecycle constraints into executable behavior. This prevents unrelated callers from mutating state arbitrarily.","principle":"State changes should occur through validated transitions.","objective":"Implement architecture-level lifecycle rules as executable constraints.","requirements":["Enumerate valid states.","Define allowed transitions.","Reject invalid transitions.","Keep transition logic centralized."],"constraints":["Some workflows require guarded transitions based on additional context.","State machines can become too rigid if the domain actually permits flexible state composition."],"preconditions":["Lifecycle states and transition rules are defined."],"input":"Current state and requested transition.","output":"New state or typed transition error.","expected_behavior":"Only defined transitions are accepted.","incorrect_code":"order.status = requested_status","corrected_code":"class Order:\n    transitions = {"draft": {"submitted"}, "submitted": {"approved", "rejected"}}\n    def transition(self, target):\n        if target not in self.transitions.get(self.status, set()):\n            raise InvalidTransition(self.status, target)\n        self.status = target","failure_mode":"Invalid lifecycle states can be created through direct mutation.","expected_error":"InvalidTransition.","cause":"State field is directly writable without transition validation.","root_cause":"Lifecycle architecture was not translated into an executable state boundary.","solution":"Centralize state transitions and enforce the transition graph.","edge_case":"Concurrent transitions require additional concurrency control; state-machine validation alone does not prevent races.","security_implication":"Unauthorized or invalid state transitions can expose restricted capabilities.","performance_implication":"Transition validation is normally inexpensive; complex guards may add computation.","test_case":"Attempt every defined valid transition and representative invalid transitions.","test_input":"State-transition matrix.","expected_test_result":"All allowed transitions succeed and disallowed transitions fail.","testing_guidance":"Use table-driven tests to cover the transition matrix.","verification_method":"Compare observed transitions with the declared transition graph.","verification_guidance":"Verify no public path can bypass transition validation.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":["Domain model implementation"],"execution_requirements":["Runtime supporting the domain model"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.98,"related_records":["D35-B005-R01","D35-B013-R01"],"depends_on":["D35-B005-R01"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":["D35-B005-R01"],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["D35-B005-R01"],"tests":["D35-B014-R04"],"verifies":["D35-B014-R05"],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Established finite-state-machine implementation pattern"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B014-R02","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"State Machine Implementation","subtopic":"Transition guards","concept":"A transition may require guards based on current facts, actor authority, or domain invariants in addition to the state graph.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"How should guarded state transitions be implemented?","answer":"Evaluate required domain guards before committing the transition and keep authorization checks distinct from pure state validity when their responsibilities differ.","explanation":"A state graph answers whether a transition is structurally possible; guards answer whether it is valid under current conditions.","principle":"Separate structural transition validity from contextual eligibility.","objective":"Prevent transitions that are structurally allowed but contextually invalid.","requirements":["Evaluate required invariants before state change.","Preserve authorization responsibility at the appropriate application boundary.","Commit state change only after guards succeed."],"constraints":["Guards must use consistent state.","External calls inside a transaction require deliberate design."],"preconditions":["Transition rules and guard conditions are defined."],"input":"Current state, requested transition, domain context.","output":"Committed transition or typed rejection.","expected_behavior":"Transition occurs only when all required guards pass.","incorrect_code":"def approve(order):\n    order.status = "approved"\n    if not order.payment_valid:\n        raise ValueError("invalid payment")","corrected_code":"def approve(order):\n    if not order.payment_valid:\n        raise InvalidTransition("payment is not valid")\n    order.transition("approved")","failure_mode":"State is mutated before a required guard succeeds.","expected_error":"InvalidTransition or domain-specific guard failure.","cause":"Validation occurs after mutation.","root_cause":"Transition implementation lacks precondition enforcement.","solution":"Evaluate all required guards before changing state.","edge_case":"Guard inputs may become stale between evaluation and commit under concurrency.","security_implication":"Authorization must not be inferred solely from a state guard.","performance_implication":"Complex guard evaluation can increase transition latency.","test_case":"Attempt a guarded transition with each required precondition false.","test_input":"Invalid payment or missing prerequisite.","expected_test_result":"State remains unchanged.","testing_guidance":"Assert both rejection and state preservation.","verification_method":"Pre/post state comparison under failed guards.","verification_guidance":"Verify no partial mutation occurs before rejection.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":["State machine implementation","Domain invariants"],"execution_requirements":["Domain runtime"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.97,"related_records":["D35-B014-R01","D35-B005-R01"],"depends_on":["D35-B014-R01"],"requires":["D35-B005-R01"],"extends":[],"refines":["D35-B014-R01"],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":[],"tests":["D35-B014-R04"],"verifies":["D35-B014-R05"],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Established guarded-state-transition practice"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B014-R03","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"State Machine Implementation","subtopic":"Transition history","concept":"Important state transitions should produce durable history when auditability or reconstruction is part of the architecture.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"When should a state transition implementation record transition history?","answer":"Record transition history when the architecture requires auditability, accountability, debugging, reconstruction, or downstream event processing.","explanation":"Current state alone may not reveal how an entity reached that state. A transition record can preserve actor, reason, previous state, new state, and timestamp according to the system's audit requirements.","principle":"Persist historical evidence when current state alone cannot satisfy required traceability.","objective":"Make significant lifecycle transitions reconstructable.","requirements":["Record previous and new states.","Capture required actor/context information.","Ensure history is written consistently with the transition where atomicity is required."],"constraints":["Do not store unnecessary sensitive data.","History retention must follow applicable requirements."],"preconditions":["Audit/history requirements are defined."],"input":"Validated state transition and audit context.","output":"New state plus transition-history record where required.","expected_behavior":"The transition and required history have consistent outcomes.","incorrect_code":"order.status = "approved"\nlogger.info("approved")","corrected_code":"with uow.transaction():\n    previous = order.status\n    order.transition("approved")\n    uow.history.record(order.id, previous, order.status, actor_id)","failure_mode":"Current state changes but durable transition history is missing or inconsistent.","expected_error":"History persistence error or transaction failure.","cause":"Audit history is treated as a non-du