{"record_id":"D35-B014-R04","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"State Machine Implementation","subtopic":"Transition matrix testing","concept":"A transition matrix provides systematic coverage of valid and invalid lifecycle transitions.","knowledge_type":"TEST","question":"How should a state machine transition matrix be tested?","answer":"Generate or enumerate tests for every declared valid transition and representative invalid transitions from each state.","explanation":"Lifecycle correctness depends on both acceptance of valid paths and rejection of invalid paths. Matrix-based tests reduce the chance that an allowed or forbidden edge is missed.","principle":"Test the transition graph as a graph, not as isolated examples.","objective":"Detect incomplete or overly permissive transition implementations.","requirements":["Cover every allowed transition.","Cover invalid targets for each relevant state.","Verify state remains unchanged after rejection."],"constraints":["Large state machines may require generated test cases.","Guard conditions need separate coverage from structural edges."],"preconditions":["Transition graph is explicitly represented."],"input":"State-transition matrix and guard rules.","output":"Pass/fail evidence for transition coverage.","expected_behavior":"Observed transition behavior matches the declared graph.","incorrect_code":"assert service.transition("approved")","corrected_code":"for state, allowed in transitions.items():\n    for target in allowed:\n        assert machine.from_state(state).transition(target).state == target\n    for target in invalid_targets(state, allowed):\n        assert_rejected(machine.from_state(state), target)","failure_mode":"Tests cover only the happy path.","expected_error":"Assertion failure for missing or forbidden transitions.","cause":"No systematic transition coverage.","root_cause":"Lifecycle implementation was tested through scenario examples rather than the declared gr