{"record_id":"D35-B015-R02","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Domain Event Implementation","subtopic":"Event contract","concept":"A domain event contract should carry stable facts required by its consumers without coupling consumers to mutable domain objects.","knowledge_type":"CONCEPT","question":"What should a domain event contain?","answer":"It should contain the stable facts necessary to understand the domain occurrence, including identity, relevant values, occurrence metadata, and version information when required.","explanation":"Passing live domain objects couples consumers to internal implementation and can expose mutable state. Explicit event data creates a stable boundary.","principle":"Publish facts through explicit contracts rather than internal object graphs.","objective":"Create maintainable event boundaries.","requirements":["Stable event identity or correlation where required.","Explicit payload fields.","Defined schema/version semantics."],"constraints":["Do not include fields solely for speculative consumers.","Sensitive information should be minimized."],"preconditions":["Consumer requirements are understood."],"input":"Domain occurrence facts.","output":"Versioned event contract.","expected_behavior":"Consumers can interpret the event without depending on aggregate internals.","incorrect_code":"OrderApproved(order=aggregate)","corrected_code":"OrderApproved(order_id=aggregate.id, total=aggregate.total, version=1)","failure_mode":"Consumers become coupled to internal aggregate structure.","expected_error":"Schema or compatibility failures after domain-model changes.","cause":"Event contains mutable implementation objects.","root_cause":"Domain model and event contract boundaries were conflated.","solution":"Map domain state to explicit event data.","edge_case":"Large aggregates may contain fields unnecessary for consumers; publish only required facts.","security_implication":"Explicit schemas make sensitive