ude information-disclosure controls.","performance_implication":"Verification overhead is primarily test execution and maintenance.","test_case":"Verify all documented error categories through representative failures.","test_input":"Failure matrix.","expected_test_result":"All mapped categories and unknown-failure behavior conform.","testing_guidance":"Keep evidence tied to dependency and application versions.","verification_method":"Failure-matrix conformance plus response-contract verification.","verification_guidance":"Mark dependency mappings as unverified when their runtime version has not been tested.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":["Error taxonomy","Test framework"],"execution_requirements":["Representative application environment"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_VERIFICATION_PATTERN","confidence":0.98,"related_records":["D35-B019-R01","D35-B019-R04"],"depends_on":["D35-B019-R04"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":["D35-B019-R01"],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":[],"tests":["D35-B019-R04"],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Established application error-contract verification practice"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B020-R01","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Error Translation Boundary","subtopic":"Infrastructure-to-application mapping","concept":"An error translation boundary converts infrastructure-specific failures into stable application semantics at the adapter or application boundary.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"Where should infrastructure exceptions be translated into application errors?","answer":"Translate them at the boundary where infrastructure knowledge ends and application semantics begin, typically inside an adapter or application-facing repository/service boundary.","explanation":"Keeping translation close to the infrastructure prevents vendor-specific exceptions from spreading through application code.","principle":"Translate errors at the architectural boundary that owns the dependency-specific knowledge.","objective":"Keep application code independent from infrastructure exception hierarchies.","requirements":["Identify infrastructure-specific failures.","Map them to application-level semantics.","Preserve causal information internally when useful."],"constraints":["Mappings must be evidence-backed and version-aware.","Not every infrastructure failure has a safe automatic application mapping."],"preconditions":["Infrastructure adapter boundary exists."],"input":"Infrastructure exception.","output":"Application-level exception or controlled internal failure.","expected_behavior":"Application callers receive stable semantic errors independent of infrastructure implementation.","incorrect_code":"try:\n    db.insert(record)\nexcept DatabaseIntegrityError:\n    raise","corrected_code":"try:\n    db.insert(record)\nexcept DatabaseIntegrityError as exc:\n    raise ConflictError("record already exists") from exc","failure_mode":"Vendor/database-specific exception leaks into application and transport layers.","expected_error":"Application-specific error after translation.","cause":"No explicit exception translation boundary.","root_cause":"Dependency implementation details crossed the architecture boundary.","solution":"Map known infrastructure failures inside the adapter or designated translation boundary.","edge_case":"One infrastructure exception may represent multiple application semantics depending on operation context.","security_implication":"Translated errors should not expose raw database statements or infrastructure details.","performance_implication":"Translation is inexpensive but excessive stack wrapping can complicate diagnostics.","test_case":"Trigger a known adapter exception and verify application-level error type.","test_input":"Duplicate persistence operation.","expected_test_result":"ConflictError reaches the application boundary with no raw database exception exposed externally.","testing_guidance":"Test adapter mappings with the dependency versions actually supported.","verification_method":"Exception-boundary inspection and integration test.","verification_guidance":"Verify causal chain remains available internally while external contract stays stable.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":["Infrastructure adapter","Application error taxonomy"],"execution_requirements":["Representative infrastructure dependency"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B007-R01","D35-B019-R01"],"depends_on":["D35-B007-R01","D35-B019-R01"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":["D35-B019-R01"],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["D35-B007-R01"],"tests":["D35-B020-R04"],"verifies":["D35-B020-R05"],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Established anti-corruption and exception-translation boundary pattern"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B020-R02","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Error Translation Boundary","subtopic":"Context-sensitive mapping","concept":"Some infrastructure failures require operation context before they can be translated safely into an application semantic.","knowledge_type":"CONCEPT","question":"Why can one infrastructure exception require different application mappings?","answer":"The same low-level failure can arise from different application operations with different meanings, so translation may require operation context rather than exception type alone.","explanation":"A database constraint failure could indicate duplicate identity in one operation and an invariant violation in another. Blind global mappings can therefore misclassify failures.","principle":"Error meaning is determined by both cause and operation context.","objective":"Avoid incorrect semantic error translation.","requirements":["Consider operation semantics when needed.","Keep mappings explicit.","Preserve unknown ambiguity rather than inventing certainty."],"constraints":["Context-sensitive mappings increase adapter complexity.","Overly broad contextual logic can become difficult to maintain."],"preconditions":["Infrastructure exception and operation context are available."],"input":"Low-level failure plus operation context.","output":"Contextually correct application error.","expected_behavior":"Application category reflects the actual operation semantics.","incorrect_code":"except IntegrityError:\n    raise ConflictError()","corrected_code":"except IntegrityError as exc:\n    if operation == "create_unique_resource":\n        raise ConflictError() from exc\n    raise InternalApplicationError() from exc","failure_mode":"All integrity failures are classified as conflicts.","expected_error":"Incorrect application error classification.","cause":"Mapping uses exception type without operation semantics.","root_cause":"Infrastructure and application failure models were assumed to be one-to-one.","solution":"Use explicit contextual mappings and preserve ambiguity when evidence is insufficient.","edge_case":"Dependency versions can alter which low-level exception is emitted for the same condition.","security_implication":"Incorrectly classifying authorization-related failures can expose information or permit unsafe retries.","performance_implication":"Contextual classification adds small control-flow overhead.","test_case":"Trigger the same infrastructure exception through two operations with different semantic meanings.","test_input":"Two operations producing one low-level error class.","expected_test_result":"Each operation receives its correct application-level classification.","testing_guidance":"Build a mapping matrix by operation and infrastructure failure.","verification_method":"Context-sensitive error mapping tests.","verification_guidance":"Verify mappings against supported dependency versions.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":["Infrastructure adapter","Application error model"],"execution_requirements":["Representative dependency behavior"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.96,"related_records":["D35-B019-R02","D35-B020-R01","D35-B020-R03"],"depends_on":["D35-B019-R02"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":["D35-B020-R01"],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":[],"tests":["D35-B020-R04"],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Established context-sensitive exception-mapping practice"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B020-R03","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Error Translation Boundary","subtopic":"Diagnostic preservation","concept":"Error translation should preserve enough internal diagnostic context for root-cause analysis without exposing sensitive implementation details externally.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"How should diagnostic context survive error translation?","answer":"Use causal exception chaining, structured internal diagnostics, and correlation identifiers while keeping external error contracts limited to safe semantic information.","explanation":"Replacing an infrastructure exception with a generic application error can otherwise destroy useful debugging evidence. Internal observability and external safety should be handled separately.","principle":"Preserve diagnostic causality internally while minimizing external disclosure.","objective":"Maintain debuggability without leaking infrastructure details.","requirements":["Preserve causal chain internally.","Attach correlation context.","Sanitize external responses."],"constraints":["Logs and traces must follow data-minimization requirements.","Do not expose raw exception text to untrusted callers."],"preconditions":["Centralized error boundary and observability mechanism exist."],"input":"Translated application error and original cause.","output":"Safe external error plus internally traceable diagnostic context.","expected_behavior":"Operators can trace the root cause while callers receive only the intended error contract.","incorrect_code":"except DBError as exc:\n    return {"error": str(exc)}","corrected_code":"except DBError as exc:\n    logger.exception("database failure", extra={"operation": operation})\n    raise InternalApplicationError("request failed") from exc","failure_mode":"Sensitive database details leak externally or root cause is lost internally.","expected_error":"Controlled application error.","cause":"External response uses raw infrastructure exception text.","root_cause":"Diagnostic and presentation responsibilities were not separated.","solution":"Chain causes internally, log structured context safely, and expose stable public errors.","edge_case":"Some clients may require a correlation ID to report a failure without receiving internal diagnostics.","security_implication":"Raw exception text can expose schema, paths, queries, credentials, or infrastructure topology.","performance_implication":"Structured logging adds I/O and serialization cost; asynchronous logging may be appropriate for high-volume systems.","test_case":"Trigger a translated infrastructure failure and inspect both external response and internal diagnostic record.","test_input":"Synthetic database failure.","expected_test_result":"External output contains no sensitive infrastructure detail while internal evidence retains causal context.","testing_guidance":"Automate assertions against forbidden sensitive fields in error responses.","verification_method":"External response inspection plus internal log/trace correlation.","verification_guidance":"Verify diagnostic retention without exposing secrets.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":["Logging/observability system","Application error boundary"],"execution_requirements":["Application runtime with structured diagnostics"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B019-R03","D35-B020-R01","D35-B030-R01"],"depends_on":["D35-B019-R03"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":["D35-B020-R01"],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":[],"tests":["D35-B020-R04"],"verifies":["D35-B020-R05"],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Established exception-cause preservation and secure error-response practice"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","update