{"record_id":"D35-B020-R04","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Error Translation Boundary","subtopic":"Boundary testing","concept":"Error translation tests must verify both semantic mapping and information-disclosure boundaries.","knowledge_type":"TEST","question":"What should be tested at an error translation boundary?","answer":"Test known mappings, contextual mappings where applicable, unknown failures, causal preservation, and sanitized external responses.","explanation":"A translation boundary can fail in two directions: it can misclassify the error or expose too much diagnostic information. Both are implementation requirements.","principle":"Test semantic correctness and security of translated errors.","objective":"Validate stable application failures without diagnostic leakage.","requirements":["Known mapping tests.","Unknown failure test.","External response sanitization.","Diagnostic correlation test."],"constraints":["Internal logging assertions should avoid depending on unstable formatting.","Sensitive test fixtures must remain non-production secrets."],"preconditions":["Error translation and observability boundaries exist."],"input":"Representative infrastructure failures.","output":"Mapping and safety test evidence.","expected_behavior":"Application semantics are correct and external responses remain safe.","incorrect_code":"assert "database" in response.text","corrected_code":"assert response.code == "INTERNAL_ERROR"\nassert "SELECT" not in response.text\nassert correlation_id in diagnostic_context","failure_mode":"Tests require raw infrastructure details in public responses.","expected_error":"Assertion failure when mapping or sanitization is incorrect.","cause":"Public error contract is not separated from internal diagnostics.","root_cause":"Error tests encode implementation leakage as expected behavior.","solution":"Assert semantic public errors and separately inspect internal diagnostics.","edge_case":"Development environments may intentionally expose more diagnostics; production contract must be tested separately.","security_implication":"Negative assertions for secrets, queries, stack traces, and internal paths are valuable.","performance_implication":"Diagnostic capture can add test overhead but should remain deterministic.","test_case":"Trigger a known infrastructure exception and inspect both boundaries.","test_input":"Synthetic persistence failure.","expected_test_result":"Correct application error, safe public response, correlated internal diagnostic.","testing_guidance":"Run security-focused response assertions in production-equivalent configuration.","verification_method":"Boundary contract and diagnostic correlation assertions.","verification_guidance":"Verify both presence of required correlation data and absence of sensitive details.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":["Test framework","Error boundary","Observability"],"execution_requirements":["Production-equivalent error configuration"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_TESTING_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B020-R01","D35-B020-R03","D35-B020-R05"],"depends_on":["D35-B020-R03"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":[],"tests":[],"verifies":["D35-B020-R05"],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Established secure error-boundary testing practice"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
