{"record_id":"D35-B021-R001","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Input Validation Implementation","subtopic":"Boundary validation","concept":"Validate transport input before invoking application logic while keeping domain invariants authoritative.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"How should input validation be implemented at an architecture boundary?","answer":"Validate structural and representational constraints at the boundary, then enforce business invariants inside the domain or application layer.","explanation":"Boundary validation prevents malformed requests from entering the system, while domain validation prevents invalid state regardless of caller.","principle":"Validate at the earliest trustworthy boundary without duplicating domain authority.","objective":"Prevent malformed external input from reaching deeper layers.","requirements":["Define explicit input schema","Reject structurally invalid input","Preserve domain invariant enforcement"],"constraints":["Do not treat transport validation as complete business validation"],"preconditions":["A defined input contract exists"],"input":"External request payload","output":"Validated application input","expected_behavior":"Malformed input is rejected before use-case execution.","incorrect_code":"def create_user(data):\n    return repository.save(User(data["name"]))","corrected_code":"def create_user(data):\n    request = CreateUserRequest.from_dict(data)\n    request.validate()\n    return user_service.create(request)","failure_mode":"Malformed data reaches application or persistence logic.","expected_error":"ValidationError","cause":"Missing or incomplete boundary validation.","root_cause":"Input contract is not enforced before application execution.","solution":"Introduce explicit request validation and retain domain invariants.","edge_case":"A syntactically valid request violates a domain invariant.","security_implication":"Unvalidated input can increase in