{"record_id":"D35-B030-R002","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","topic":"Structured Logging Implementation","subtopic":"Correlation identifiers","concept":"Logs for one logical operation should carry a stable correlation identifier across participating components.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"How should correlation IDs be implemented in application logging?","answer":"Create or accept a validated correlation identifier at the boundary and propagate it through the operation context and structured log records.","explanation":"Correlation allows distributed or multi-step execution to be reconstructed.","principle":"A logical operation needs a stable observability identity.","objective":"Connect related events without relying on message text.","requirements":["Correlation ID generation/validation","Request-scoped propagation","Structured field"],"constraints":["Do not trust arbitrary correlation values for authorization"],"preconditions":["Request context exists"],"input":"Incoming request","output":"Correlated log events","expected_behavior":"All events for the logical operation carry the same correlation ID.","incorrect_code":"logger.info("started")\nworker.log("finished")","corrected_code":"context = RequestContext(correlation_id=correlation_id)\nlogger.info("started", extra={"correlation_id": context.correlation_id})\nworker.log("finished", extra={"correlation_id": context.correlation_id})","failure_mode":"Related events cannot be reliably connected.","expected_error":"CorrelationContextMissing","cause":"No propagation mechanism.","root_cause":"Correlation treated as logger-local metadata.","solution":"Include correlation ID in request/task context.","edge_case":"A workflow intentionally creates child correlation IDs.","security_implication":"Correlation IDs should not contain sensitive identifiers.","performance_implication":"Adding a small field to each event has low overhead but high-volume systems should account for serialization cost.","test_case":"Execute multi-step operation and inspect all events.","test_input":"Single operation with three components","expected_test_result":"All related events share expected correlation identifier.","testing_guidance":"Test synchronous, asynchronous, and background propagation.","verification_method":"End-to-end observability test.","verification_guidance":"Verify no event in the operation loses or incorrectly changes the correlation ID.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"None","framework_version":null,"dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":[],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_OBSERVABILITY_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B024-R002","D35-B030-R001","D35-B031-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B024-R002"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["correlation_id_propagation"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":"Established correlation-context observability practice.","created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B030-R003","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","topic":"Structured Logging Implementation","subtopic":"Sensitive-data redaction","concept":"Structured logging must apply field-level redaction or allowlisting before events leave the application process.","knowledge_type":"SECURITY","question":"How should sensitive values be prevented from entering structured logs?","answer":"Define approved log fields and redact or exclude sensitive values before serialization.","explanation":"Structured logs make fields easier to aggregate, but they can also make accidental leakage systematic.","principle":"Observability data requires the same data-minimization discipline as application data.","objective":"Prevent secret and sensitive-data leakage through logs.","requirements":["Field classification","Redaction policy","Automated leakage tests"],"constraints":["Do not rely solely on developer awareness"],"preconditions":["Structured logging exists"],"input":"Event containing sensitive value","output":"Sanitized log event","expected_behavior":"Sensitive value is absent or replaced according to policy.","incorrect_code":"logger.info("login", extra={"password": password, "token": token})","corrected_code":"logger.info("login", extra={"user_id": user_id, "auth_result": "success"})","failure_mode":"Credentials or sensitive data are logged.","expected_error":"SensitiveLogData","cause":"No logging allowlist/redaction.","root_cause":"Logging schema did not classify protected fields.","solution":"Use approved-field schemas and redaction controls.","edge_case":"Nested exception or object stringification leaks a secret.","security_implication":"Logs can become a secondary credential/data-exposure channel.","performance_implication":"Redaction adds per-event processing cost.","test_case":"Emit event containing synthetic secret and inspect serialized output.","test_input":"Synthetic secret in event payload","expected_test_result":"Secret does not appear in log output.","