{"record_id":"D35-B046-R001","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Concurrency Implementation","subtopic":"Shared State","concept":"Concurrency-safe state ownership","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should shared mutable state be implemented when multiple operations can access it concurrently?","answer":"Assign explicit ownership and synchronize access or redesign the state so operations do not require unsafe shared mutation.","explanation":"Architecture must identify which component owns mutable state and what concurrency mechanism protects it. Accidental shared mutation creates race conditions.","principle":"Mutable state requires an explicit ownership and synchronization model.","objective":"Prevent race conditions and lost updates.","requirements":["State ownership","Synchronization or serialization policy","Atomic update semantics"],"constraints":["Locks should protect the minimum required critical section","Lock ordering must avoid deadlocks"],"preconditions":["Concurrent access exists"],"input":"Concurrent state operations.","output":"Consistent state transition.","expected_behavior":"Concurrent operations preserve defined invariants.","incorrect_code":"counter = 0\n\ndef increment():\n    global counter\n    counter += 1","corrected_code":"from threading import Lock\n\ncounter = 0\nlock = Lock()\n\ndef increment():\n    global counter\n    with lock:\n        counter += 1","failure_mode":"Concurrent updates can be lost or violate invariants.","expected_error":"Race-dependent incorrect state.","cause":"Unsynchronized mutable state.","root_cause":"No explicit concurrency ownership model.","solution":"Use synchronization or redesign state ownership.","edge_case":"Multiple processes access the same logical state; an in-process lock is insufficient.","security_implication":"Race conditions in authorization or quota state can create security violations.","performance_implication":"Synchronization can reduce concurrency; measure contention under representative workloads.","test_case":"Run many concurrent increments and compare final state with expected count.","test_input":"Concurrent increment operations.","expected_test_result":"Final state matches expected result when the implementation and execution environment support the synchronization model.","testing_guidance":"Use stress tests in addition to deterministic unit tests.","verification_method":"Concurrency test plus state invariant assertion.","verification_guidance":"Do not infer race safety from a single successful run.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.x","framework":"none","framework_version":"none","version_range":"Python 3.x","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":"Python 3.x","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"DOCUMENTED_STANDARD","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B013-R001","D35-B014-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B013-R001"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":["unsynchronized_shared_state"],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["concurrency_safe_state"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Python threading documentation","Concurrency control principles"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B046-R002","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Concurrency Implementation","subtopic":"Optimistic Update","concept":"Version-checked state update","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should an implementation detect concurrent modification before overwriting state?","answer":"Load state with a version or revision, perform the update conditionally on that version, and reject the update if another writer changed the state first.","explanation":"Optimistic concurrency converts an implicit race into an explicit conflict that the application can handle.","principle":"Concurrent modifications should be detected at the state ownership boundary.","objective":"Prevent lost updates.","requirements":["Revision field","Conditional update","Conflict result"],"constraints":["Conflict resolution policy must be defined","A version number alone does not solve cross-system consistency"],"preconditions":["Persistence layer supports conditional updates or equivalent compare-and-swap semantics"],"input":"Entity identifier, expected version, proposed update.","output":"Updated entity or concurrency conflict.","expected_behavior":"Update succeeds only when the expected version remains current.","incorrect_code":"entity = repository.load(id)\nentity.name = new_name\nrepository.save(entity)","corrected_code":"entity = repository.load(id)\nexpected_version = entity.version\nentity.name = new_name\nrepository.save_if_version(entity, expected_version)","failure_mode":"Second writer silently overwrites first writer.","expected_error":"ConcurrencyConflict on stale version.","cause":"Unconditional save.","root_cause":"No optimistic concurrency boundary.","solution":"Condition persistence update on the loaded revision.","edge_case":"A conflict requires semantic merge rather than simple retry.","security_implication":"Authorization decisions based on stale state can become invalid after concurrent changes.","performance_implicati