{"record_id":"D35-B047-R002","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Serialization Boundary","subtopic":"Schema Evolution","concept":"Versioned serialized payload","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should serialized payload schemas evolve across application versions?","answer":"Use explicit schema versions or compatibility rules and make readers tolerant only within documented compatibility boundaries.","explanation":"A producer and consumer may not deploy simultaneously. Serialization contracts therefore require an evolution strategy independent of source-code versioning.","principle":"Serialized data is a contract with an independent lifecycle.","objective":"Prevent deployment-order failures during schema evolution.","requirements":["Schema version policy","Compatibility rules","Reader/writer tests"],"constraints":["Tolerant readers must not accept semantically invalid data","Removing fields may require migration or versioning"],"preconditions":["Serialized payloads persist or cross deployment boundaries"],"input":"Payload generated by one software version and consumed by another.","output":"Parsed domain/application representation or controlled incompatibility error.","expected_behavior":"Supported version combinations deserialize according to documented rules.","incorrect_code":"def parse(payload):\n    return User(name=payload['name'], role=payload['role'])","corrected_code":"def parse(payload):\n    version = payload.get('schema_version', 1)\n    if version == 1:\n        return parse_v1(payload)\n    if version == 2:\n        return parse_v2(payload)\n    raise UnsupportedSchemaVersion(version)","failure_mode":"New consumer cannot read older persisted payload.","expected_error":"UnsupportedSchemaVersion or controlled validation error.","cause":"No schema lifecycle policy.","root_cause":"Source version assumed to equal data version.","solution":"Version and test serialized contracts explicitly.","edge_case":"P