{"record_id":"D35-B050-R001","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Architecture-to-Implementation Integration","subtopic":"End-to-End Boundary","concept":"Thin-adapter end-to-end path","knowledge_type":"integration_implementation","question":"How should an end-to-end implementation verify that architecture boundaries are actually wired together?","answer":"Exercise a representative external entry point through the adapter, application boundary, domain logic, and infrastructure adapter using controlled dependencies.","explanation":"Unit tests can pass while composition wiring is broken. A representative end-to-end path verifies that architectural components actually connect as designed.","principle":"Architecture must be validated both structurally and through representative runtime paths.","objective":"Verify real component composition without requiring production infrastructure.","requirements":["Representative entry point","Application orchestration","Controlled infrastructure","Observable result"],"constraints":["End-to-end tests should remain focused on architecture wiring rather than duplicate every unit case"],"preconditions":["Components and interfaces are implemented"],"input":"Representative external request.","output":"Expected external response or result.","expected_behavior":"Request crosses the intended architecture layers and returns the expected outcome.","incorrect_code":"def handler(request):\n    return repository.save(request.body)","corrected_code":"def handler(request, use_case):\n    command = map_request(request)\n    result = use_case.execute(command)\n    return map_response(result)","failure_mode":"External adapter bypasses application orchestration.","expected_error":"Integration assertion or architecture test failure.","cause":"Incorrect dependency wiring.","root_cause":"End-to-end boundary path was never verified.","solution":"Add representative end-to-end composition tests.","edge_case":"Infrastructu