{"record_id":"D35-B050-R002","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Architecture-to-Implementation Integration","subtopic":"Dependency Replacement","concept":"Runtime adapter replacement","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should an architecture allow an infrastructure adapter to be replaced without changing application logic?","answer":"Define the dependency through a stable port and assemble the concrete adapter at the composition root.","explanation":"Replaceability is demonstrated when application code remains unchanged while infrastructure implementation changes through dependency injection.","principle":"Concrete technology choices belong outside the stable application contract.","objective":"Validate infrastructure replaceability.","requirements":["Stable port","Concrete adapter implementations","Composition-root injection"],"constraints":["Adapters must satisfy the same semantic contract","Replacement does not imply identical performance or feature sets"],"preconditions":["Port contract is defined"],"input":"Application and alternative infrastructure implementations.","output":"Application operating against selected adapter.","expected_behavior":"Application behavior remains contract-compatible when adapter is replaced.","incorrect_code":"class UserService:\n    def init(self):\n        self.repo = PostgresUserRepository()","corrected_code":"class UserService:\n    def init(self, repo):\n        self.repo = repo","failure_mode":"Application service is coupled to one infrastructure technology.","expected_error":"Replacement requires source modification.","cause":"Concrete dependency constructed inside application service.","root_cause":"Composition root boundary is missing.","solution":"Inject the repository through the application port.","edge_case":"Alternative adapters expose different capabilities that are not part of the common contract.","security_implication":"Every adapter must enforce the security se