{"record_id":"D35-B050-R003","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Architecture-to-Implementation Integration","subtopic":"Configuration Wiring","concept":"Environment-independent application composition","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should runtime configuration be kept separate from application construction logic?","answer":"Load and validate configuration once at the composition boundary, then inject typed configuration into components that require it.","explanation":"Reading environment variables throughout application code creates hidden dependencies and makes behavior difficult to test.","principle":"Runtime configuration should be resolved at the boundary and passed explicitly inward.","objective":"Make application composition deterministic and testable.","requirements":["Typed configuration object","Single resolution boundary","Dependency injection"],"constraints":["Secrets require appropriate secure handling","Components should not independently read environment variables"],"preconditions":["Configuration schema exists"],"input":"Environment/configuration source.","output":"Validated runtime configuration object.","expected_behavior":"Components receive configuration explicitly and do not depend on ambient process state.","incorrect_code":"class EmailSender:\n    def send(self, message):\n        host = os.environ['SMTP_HOST']\n        return connect(host).send(message)","corrected_code":"class EmailSender:\n    def init(self, smtp_host):\n        self.smtp_host = smtp_host\n\n    def send(self, message):\n        return connect(self.smtp_host).send(message)","failure_mode":"Component behavior depends on hidden environment state.","expected_error":"ConfigurationError or environment-dependent behavior.","cause":"Configuration read inside component.","root_cause":"Configuration boundary not centralized.","solution":"Resolve configuration at startup and inject validated values.","edge_case":"Dynamic configuration intentionally changes at runtime and therefore requires a dedicated configuration-update mechanism.","security_implication":"Centralized configuration handling makes secret access easier to audit and restrict.","performance_implication":"Startup resolution avoids repeated environment parsing; dynamic configuration may require caching and synchronization.","test_case":"Construct EmailSender with a test host without modifying process environment.","test_input":"smtp_host='test.local'.","expected_test_result":"Component uses injected configuration.","testing_guidance":"Unit-test components with explicit configuration values.","verification_method":"Composition test plus static search for ambient configuration access.","verification_guidance":"Verify application components do not directly read environment variables unless explicitly designated as boundary adapters.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.x","framework":"none","framework_version":"none","version_range":"Python 3.x","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":"Python 3.x","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B031-R001","D35-B008-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B031-R001","D35-B008-R001"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":["configuration_injection"],"contrasts_with":["ambient_configuration_access"],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["environment_independent_composition"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["The Twelve-Factor App, Config","Dependency injection principles"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B050-R004","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Architecture-to-Implementation Integration","subtopic":"Operational Contract","concept":"Runtime configuration and health integration","knowledge_type":"integration_implementation","question":"How should configuration validation and runtime health checks work together during startup?","answer":"Validate required configuration before starting dependent components, then expose readiness only after required resources are initialized and usable according to the application's health policy.","explanation":"A process can be alive while not being ready to serve correct traffic. Configuration validation and readiness are related lifecycle gates but represent different conditions.","principle":"Startup validity and runtime readiness are explicit lifecycle states.","objective":"Prevent traffic from reaching incompletely initialized components.","requirements":["Configuration validation","Initialization sequencing","Readiness state","Failure reporting"],"constraints":["Not every optional dependency should block readiness","Readiness checks must reflect actual serving capability"],"preconditions":["Application exposes a health/readiness contract"],"input":"Startup configuration and dependency initialization results.","output":"Ready or not-ready runtime state.","expected_behavior":"Application reports readiness only when required initialization conditions are satisfied.","incorrect_code":"def start():\n    server.start()\n    initialize_database()","corrected_code":"def start():\n    config.validate()\n    database.initialize()\n    readiness.mark_ready()\n    server.start()","failure_mode":"Server accepts work before required dependencies are initialized.","expected_error":"Startup request failures or incorrect readiness signal.","cause":"Initialization and readiness are unordered.","root_cause":"Lifecycle state is not modeled explicitly.","solution":"Validate configuration, initialize required dependencies, then transition to ready state.","edge_case":"Server must bind before readiness can be externally observed; readiness endpoint should remain not-ready until initialization completes.","security_implication":"Serving requests before security-critical configuration or identity dependencies initialize can create unsafe behavior.","performance_implication":"Startup readiness gating affects deployment rollout duration but should not be optimized by skipping required checks.","test_case":"Start application with dependency initialization failure and inspect readiness.","test_input":"Database initialization failure.","expected_test_result":"Application does not report ready.","testing_guidance":"Test success, required dependency failure, and optional dependency degradation.","verification_method":"Startup integration test plus readiness contract test.","verification_guidance":"Verify readiness state transitions occur only after required initialization.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.x","framework":"none","framework_version":"none","version_range":"Application dependent","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":"Application lifecycle implementation","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B031-R004","D35-B039-R001","D35-B039-R002"],"depends_on":["D35-B031-R004","D35-B039-R001"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":["D35-B039-R001"],"specializes":["startup_readiness_integration"],"contrasts_with":["premature_readiness"],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["configuration_readiness_gate"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Kubernetes liveness/readiness probe concepts","Google SRE service startup principles"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B050-R005","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Architecture-to-Implementation Integration","subtopic":"Final Architecture Gate","concept":"Architecture implementation acceptance gate","knowledge_type":"verification","question":"What should an architecture-to-implementation acceptance gate verify before an implementation is considered complete?","answer":"Verify structural dependency rules, interface contracts, application orchestration, lifecycle behavior, failure handling, security boundaries, representative runtime wiring, and automated regression tests.","explanation":"A component can be individually correct while the architecture is incorrectly wired. Acceptance therefore requires both static and dynamic evidence.","principle":"Architecture implementation is complete only when intended structure and representative behavior are both verified.","objective":"Prevent architecture-complete claims based only on source existence or unit-test success.","requirements":["Structural verification","Contract verification","Integration verification","Failure-path verification","Security boundary verification","Regression protection"],"constraints":["Evidence must distinguish executed tests from illustrative examples","Not every possible runtime state can be exhaustively tested"],"preconditions":["Architecture specification and implementation exist"],"input":"Architecture rules, source tree, tests, and representative runtime paths.","output":"Architecture implementation acceptance result.","expected_behavior":"Implementation passes defined structural and behavioral gates or records explicit unresolved gaps.","incorrect_code":"assert files_exist()\nassert unit_tests_passed","corrected_code":"assert dependency_rules_pass()\nassert contract_tests_pass()\nassert integration_paths_pass()\nassert failure_paths_pass()\nassert security_boundaries_pass()","failure_mode":"Implementation is accepted because files and basic tests exist while architecture wiring remains unverified.","expected_error":"Architecture acceptance failure.","cause":"Acceptance gate checks presence rather than architecture behavior.","root_cause":"No explicit architecture-to-runtime verification contract.","solution":"Use a multi-gate acceptance process with evidence-backed results.","edge_case":"A gate cannot execute because an external dependency is unavailable; status must remain unverified rather than being marked passed.","security_implication":"Security boundary verification must be explicit and cannot be inferred from general functional tests.","performance_implication":"Comprehensive architecture gates increase validation time; gate selection should prioritize architectural risk while preserving required coverage.","test_case":"Run acceptance against an implementation with one intentionally broken dependency direction and one broken integration path.","test_input":"Partially non-compliant implementation.","expected_test_result":"Acceptance fails and identifies the unresolved gates.","testing_guidance":"Track each gate independently with executed/not-executed evidence.","verification_method":"Combined static analysis, contract testing, integration testing, and security verification.","verification_guidance":"Do not mark a gate passed without corresponding evidence; preserve failed and unverified states.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.x","framework":"none","framework_version":"none","version_range":"Dataset and implementation dependent","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":"Architecture analysis, test suite, and representative integration environment","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B040-R005","D35-B049-R005","D35-B050-R001","D35-B050-R004"],"depends_on":["D35-B040-R005","D35-B049-R005"],"requires":[],"extends":["D35-B040-R005"],"refines":["D35-B049-R005"],"specializes":["architecture_acceptance_gate"],"contrasts_with":["file_presence_acceptance"],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["architecture_to_implementation_verification"],"tests":["D35-B049-R005"],"verifies":["D35-B050-R001","D35-B050-R004"],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Architecture fitness function principles","Software architecture verification and integration testing practices"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}

{"record_id":"D35-B051-R001","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Command Bus Implementation","subtopic":"Command dispatch boundary","concept":"A command bus provides an explicit application boundary for dispatching commands to their handlers without coupling callers to concrete handler implementations.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"How should a command bus be implemented as an architectural boundary?","answer":"Define a typed command contract, map each command type to exactly one handler, validate the command before dispatch, invoke the handler through the application boundary, and propagate a structured result or classified failure.","explanation":"The command bus should coordinate dispatch rather than contain business rules. Handler resolution belongs to composition or registration infrastructure, while authorization, transaction scope, and domain behavior remain explicit application concerns.","principle":"Dispatch infrastructure should not become an implicit business-logic container.","objective":"Implement decoupled command dispatch while preserving explicit application semantics.","requirements":["Typed command contract","Deterministic handler resolution","Explicit failure behavior","Testable dispatch path"],"constraints":["No hidden global mutable state","One authoritative handler per command type","No business rules inside dispatch infrastructure"],"preconditions":["Command type is registered","Handler dependency graph is valid"],"input":"Command object plus application execution context.","output":"Handler result or classified application failure.","expected_behavior":"The registered handler receives the command exactly once per dispatch invocation and returns its defined result.","incorrect_code":"handlers = {}\ndef dispatch(command):\n    return handlers"type(command)" (command)","corrected_code":"from dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Protocol, TypeVar, Generic\n\nC = TypeVar("C")\nR = TypeVar("R")\n\nclass Handler(Protocol, Generic[C, R]):\n    def handle(self, command: C) -> R: ...\n\nclass CommandBus:\n    def init(self, handlers: dict[type, Handler]):\n        self._handlers = dict(handlers)\n\n    def dispatch(self, command):\n        handler = self._handlers.get(type(command))\n        if handler is None:\n            raise LookupError(f"No handler for {type(command).name}")\n        return handler.handle(command)","failure_mode":"Missing or ambiguous command registration causes dispatch failure.","expected_error":"LookupError for an unregistered command type in the illustrative implementation.","cause":"Handler registry does not contain the exact command type.","root_cause":"Dispatch dependency was not explicitly registered or validated.","solution":"Validate command-handler registrations during composition and keep resolution deterministic.","edge_case":"A subclassed command may not match an exact-type registry entry; define whether inheritance-based dispatch is supported.","security_implication":"Authorization must occur before sensitive command execution; command dispatch itself is not an authorization mechanism.","performance_implication":"Registry lookup should normally be O(1); avoid dynamic reflection on every dispatch unless required.","test_case":"Dispatch a registered command and an unregistered command.","test_input":"Registered command instance followed by an unsupported command type.","expected_test_result":"Registered command reaches its handler; unsupported command produces the defined dispatch failure.","testing_guidance":"Test exact registration, duplicate registration, missing registration, handler exceptions, and context propagation.","verification_method":"Static inspection plus unit and integration tests.","verification_guidance":"Verify every supported command has one deterministic handler and failures do not silently fall through.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":null,"framework_version":null,"version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":["Python standard library typing/dataclasses"],"execution_requirements":"Python 3.11+","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.96,"related_records":["D35-B004-R001","D35-B019-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B008-R001"],"requires":[],"extends":["D35-B004-R001"],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["Command dispatch boundary"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":["Application service and command-dispatch architectural patterns"],"provenance":["Established application architecture pattern"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19","code_applicability":"CODE_RELEVANT","implementation_coverage":"IMPLEMENTATION"}

{"record_id":"D35-B051-R002","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Command Bus Implementation","subtopic":"Handler registration","concept":"Handler registration should be explicit, unique, and validated before runtime traffic reaches the command bus.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"Why should command-handler registration be validated at startup?","answer":"Startup validation detects missing or duplicate handlers before production requests depend on them, converting configuration defects into deterministic startup failures.","explanation":"Late registration failures are harder to diagnose and can appear as intermittent application errors. A composition-time registry validation makes the architecture executable and observable.","principle":"Invalid dependency composition should fail before normal request processing.","objective":"Make command dispatch configuration structurally verifiable.","requirements":["Registration API","Duplicate detection","Missing-handler detection","Startup validation"],"constraints":["Do not silently overwrite duplicate handlers","Do not defer known structural errors to first use"],"preconditions":["All supported command types are known to the composition root"],"input":"Command-handler registration set.","output":"Validated immutable dispatch registry.","expected_behavior":"Duplicate or missing required registrations prevent the application from entering a ready state.","incorrect_code":"registry[command_type] = handler","corrected_code":"def register(registry, command_type, handler):\n    if command_type in registry:\n        raise ValueError(f"Duplicate handler: {command_type.name}")\n    registry[command_type] = handler\n\n\ndef validate(registry, required_types):\n    missing = required_types - registry.keys()\n    if missing:\n        names = ", ".join(t.name for t in missing)\n        raise ValueError(f"Missing handlers: {names}")","failure_mode":"Duplicate or missing registrations are silently accepted.","expected_error":"ValueError during composition validation.","cause":"Registry mutation lacks invariant checks.","root_cause":"Dependency configuration is treated as incidental data instead of an architectural invariant.","solution":"Enforce uniqueness and completeness before readiness.","edge_case":"Optional commands must be represented separately from required commands so validation does not reject intentional extensions.","security_implication":"Unexpected handlers should not be injectable through untrusted runtime input.","performance_implication":"Validation is normally startup-only and should not materially affect steady-state dispatch.","test_case":"Register the same command twice and omit a required command.","test_input":"Duplicate command type and incomplete required set.","expected_test_result":"Both configuration errors are detected before runtime readiness.","testing_guidance":"Include startup configuration tests and registry mutation tests.","verification_method":"Composition validation and unit tests.","verification_guidance":"Assert that readiness cannot be reached with an invalid handler registry.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":null,"framework_version":null,"version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":["Python standard library"],"execution_requirements":"Python 3.11+","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.97,"related_records":["D35-B008-R001","D35-B040-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B051-R001"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":["D35-B051-R001"],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["Handler registration invariant"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":["Dependency validation and composition-root patterns"],"provenance":["Established application architecture pattern"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19","code_applicability":"CODE_RELEVANT","implementation_coverage":"IMPLEMENTATION"}

{"record_id":"D35-B051-R003","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Command Bus Implementation","subtopic":"Execution context propagation","concept":"Command dispatch should explicitly carry request-scoped context such as tenant, actor, correlation, deadline, and authorization information.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"How should request context be propagated through a command bus?","answer":"Represent required context explicitly and pass it through the application boundary instead of relying on hidden mutable globals.","explanation":"Explicit context makes command execution deterministic, testable, and compatible with concurrent requests and tenant isolation.","principle":"Request-scoped execution context must remain request-scoped.","objective":"Prevent context leakage while preserving necessary execution metadata.","requirements":["Explicit context model","Immutable or controlled context values","Tenant and actor propagation where applicable"],"constraints":["No cross-request mutable context","No implicit tenant selection from process-global state"],"preconditions":["Caller has established a valid execution context"],"input":"Command and execution context.","output":"Handler result executed under the supplied context.","expected_behavior":"The same context remains associated with the command throughout its application execution path.","incorrect_code":"CURRENT_TENANT = None\n\ndef dispatch(command):\n    return handlers[type(command)](command, CURRENT_TENANT)","corrected_code":"from dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass ExecutionContext:\n    tenant_id: str\n    actor_id: str\n    correlation_id: str\n\nclass CommandBus:\n    def init(self, handlers):\n        self.handlers = handlers\n\n    def dispatch(self, command, context: ExecutionContext):\n        return self.handlers[type(command)].handle(command, context)","failure_mode":"Concurrent executions observe another request's context.","expected_error":"Context mismatch or authorization failure.","cause":"Process-global mutable request context.","root_cause":"Architectural boundary does not model request scope explicitly.","solution":"Pass immutable request context through the command/application boundary.","edge_case":"Background jobs without a human actor require an explicit service/system actor representation.","security_implication":"Tenant and actor context must be authoritative and cannot be replaced by client-controlled identifiers.","performance_implication":"Passing a small immutable context has negligible overhead compared with application work.","test_case":"Execute two commands concurrently with different contexts.","test_input":"Command A with tenant A and command B with tenant B.","expected_test_result":"Each handler observes only its own context.","testing_guidance":"Use concurrency tests and deliberately interleave handler execution.","verification_method":"Concurrency test plus static review for global request state.","verification_guidance":"Search for mutable global context and verify all security-sensitive operations receive authoritative context.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":null,"framework_version":null,"version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":["Python standard library"],"execution_requirements":"Python 3.11+","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.98,"related_records":["D35-B026-R001","D35-B028-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B051-R001"],"requires":["D35-B026-R001"],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["Explicit execution context propagation"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":["Request-context and isolation patterns"],"provenance":["Established concurrent application design pattern"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19","code_applicability":"CODE_RELEVANT","implement