{"record_id":"D35-B069-R002","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Batch Processing Boundary","subtopic":"Chunking","concept":"Chunking divides large work into bounded units to control resource use, failure scope, and checkpoint granularity.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"How should batch chunking be implemented?","answer":"Choose chunk boundaries according to resource and transactional constraints, preserve item identity, and define behavior for incomplete chunks.","explanation":"Chunk size is an architectural parameter affecting memory, database transaction duration, retry cost, and throughput. There is no universally optimal value.","principle":"Chunking is a resource and failure-boundary decision, not merely a loop optimization.","objective":"Implement bounded batch execution.","requirements":["Explicit chunk size","Stable item identity","Partial-chunk handling","Checkpoint semantics"],"constraints":["Do not load unbounded input into memory","Do not claim an optimal chunk size without measurement"],"preconditions":["Input can be partitioned safely"],"input":"Item stream.","output":"Sequence of bounded chunks.","expected_behavior":"Each chunk remains within declared resource and transaction limits.","incorrect_code":"items = list(source)\nfor item in items:\n    process(item)","corrected_code":"from itertools import islice\n\ndef chunks(source, size):\n    iterator = iter(source)\n    while batch := list(islice(iterator, size)):\n        yield batch","failure_mode":"Memory exhaustion or oversized transaction scope.","expected_error":"Resource or processing error when limits are exceeded.","cause":"Entire input is materialized before processing.","root_cause":"No bounded chunking boundary.","solution":"Stream and partition input into controlled chunks.","edge_case":"The final chunk contains fewer items than the configured size.","security_implication":"Chunk boundaries must not accidentally mix tenant or authorization scopes when isolation requires separation.","performance_implication":"Chunk size must be measured against workload characteristics; this example makes no benchmark claim.","test_case":"Process ten items with chunk size three.","test_input":"10 items, size 3.","expected_test_result":"Chunks have sizes 3,3,3,1.","testing_guidance":"Test empty input, one item, exact multiple, remainder, and source failure mid-stream.","verification_method":"Unit tests plus resource-observation integration tests.","verification_guidance":"Verify input count equals sum of chunk counts.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":null,"framework_version":null,"version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":["Python runtime"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.98,"related_records":["D35-B069-R001","D35-B069-R003"],"depends_on":["D35-B069-R001"],"requires":[],"extends":null,"refines":null,"specializes":"Batch chunking","contrasts_with":"Unbounded materialization","contradicts":null,"supersedes":null,"implements":"Batch chunking boundary","tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":["Streaming and bounded-resource processing patterns"],"provenance":"Established streaming pattern; code illustrative and not executed.","created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19","code_applicability":"CODE_RELEVANT","implementation_coverage":["IMPLEMENTATION","EDGE-CASE","TEST","VERIFICATION","PERFORMANCE","SECURITY"]}

{"record_id":"D35-B069-R003","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Batch Processing Boundary","subtopic":"Partial Failure","concept":"A batch can complete with mixed item outcomes when its contract explicitly supports partial success and records failed items for recovery.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"How should partial batch failure be represented?","answer":"Return an aggregate result containing successful, failed, skipped, and unresolved item outcomes, with enough identity to retry or reconcile failed items.","explanation":"Binary batch success/failure is insufficient for many workloads. Partial results allow targeted recovery and accurate reporting.","principle":"Aggregate status must preserve item-level evidence.","objective":"Implement transparent partial-failure semantics.","requirements":["Item outcome categories","Stable item identity","Retry/recovery information","Aggregate status"],"constraints":["Do not silently classify skipped items as successful","Do not retry all items when only a subset failed unless policy requires it"],"preconditions":["Batch contract permits partial processing"],"input":"Items and processing results.","output":"Partial batch result.","expected_behavior":"Aggregate status accurately reflects item-level outcomes.","incorrect_code":"try:\n    process_all(items)\n    return "SUCCESS"\nexcept Exception:\n    return "FAILED"","corrected_code":"result = BatchResult()\nfor item in items:\n    try:\n        process(item)\n        result.success(item.id)\n    except RetryableError as exc:\n        result.retryable(item.id, str(exc))\n    except Exception as exc:\n        result.failed(item.id, str(exc))\nreturn result","failure_mode":"Successful items are repeated unnecessarily or failed items disappear from reporting.","expected_error":"No single error is required; aggregate status captures outcomes.","cause":"Exception handling occurs only at whole-batch level.","root_cause":"Item-level outcome semantics are absent.","solution":"Track outcomes per item and expose recovery categories.","edge_case":"An item fails after its side effect succeeded but before the result is persisted.","security_implication":"Failure records must not leak sensitive item data across tenant boundaries.","performance_implication":"Per-item outcome storage increases metadata overhead; retain only what recovery requires.","test_case":"Process five items with two retryable and one permanent failure.","test_input":"Mixed outcome batch.","expected_test_result":"Aggregate result reports two successes, two retryable, and one permanent failure.","testing_guidance":"Test each outcome category and recovery operation.","verification_method":"Unit and integration tests.","verification_guidance":"Verify aggregate totals reconcile exactly with input count.","language":"Java","language_version":"17+","framework":null,"framework_version":null,"version_range":"Java 17+","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":["JDK 17+"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.98,"related_records":["D35-B069-R001","D35-B069-R004"],"depends_on":["D35-B069-R001"],"requires":[],"extends":null,"refines":null,"specializes":"Batch partial failure","contrasts_with":"All-or-nothing batch status","contradicts":null,"supersedes":null,"implements":"Partial batch failure boundary","tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":["Batch recovery and partial-result patterns"],"provenance":"Established processing pattern; Java example illustrative and not executed.","created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19","code_applicability":"CODE_RELEVANT","implementation_coverage":["IMPLEMENTATION","EDGE-CASE","TEST","VERIFICATION","SECURITY","PERFORMANCE"]}

{"record_id":"D35-B069-R004","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Batch Processing Boundary","subtopic":"Checkpoint and Resume","concept":"Checkpointing records sufficient progress to resume a large batch without repeating completed work beyond the declared idempotency policy.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"How should batch checkpointing be implemented?","answer":"Persist a checkpoint based on stable item identity or source position together with enough metadata to detect input changes and recovery boundaries.","explanation":"A numeric offset alone can be unsafe when the source changes between runs. Stable identities and snapshot semantics are preferable when available.","principle":"Resume from stable evidence, not ambiguous positions.","objective":"Implement recoverable batch processing.","requirements":["Stable checkpoint identity","Input snapshot/version where needed","Checkpoint persistence","Recovery policy"],"constraints":["Do not assume source offsets remain stable","Do not mark an item complete before its required side effect is durably established"],"preconditions":["Batch workload requires restartability"],"input":"Batch state and checkpoint.","output":"Updated checkpoint.","expected_behavior":"Restart resumes from a safe boundary without silently skipping items.","incorrect_code":"checkpoint = index\nsave(checkpoint)\nprocess(item)","corrected_code":"process(item)\ncheckpoint = item.id\nsave_checkpoint(checkpoint)","failure_mode":"Checkpoint advances before processing, causing item loss after crash.","expected_error":"CheckpointIntegrityError when checkpoint state cannot be reconciled with input.","cause":"Checkpoint is persisted before required work completes.","root_cause":"Progress evidence is not ordered with the side effect.","solution":"Define checkpoint commit semantics and stable item identity.","edge_case":"Processing succeeds but checkpoint persistence fails; recovery may repeat the item and therefore requires idempotency or reconciliation.","security_implication":"Checkpoint data must preserve tenant scope and avoid exposing sensitive item content.","performance_implication":"Frequent checkpoints improve recovery granularity but add persistence overhead.","test_case":"Crash before processing, after processing, and after checkpoint persistence.","test_input":"Three crash positions.","expected_test_result":"Recovery behavior matches the declared checkpoint and idempotency contract.","testing_guidance":"Inject failures around every checkpoint boundary.","verification_method":"Crash-recovery integration tests.","verification_guidance":"Verify no item is silently skipped and repeated items are safe where required.","language":"Go","language_version":"1.22+","framework":null,"framework_version":null,"version_range":"Go 1.22+","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":["Go toolchain and durable checkpoint store"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B069-R003","D35-B012-R001","D35-B017-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B069-R001"],"requires":["Stable item identity","Durable checkpoint store"],"extends":null,"refines":null,"specializes":"Batch checkpointing","contrasts_with":null,"contradicts":null,"supersedes":null,"implements":"Batch recovery boundary","tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":["Checkpoint and recovery patterns"],"provenance":"Established recoverable-processing pattern; Go example illustrative and not executed.","created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19","code_applicability":"CODE_RELEVANT","implementation_coverage":["IMPLEMENTATION","EDGE-CASE","TEST","VERIFICATION","SECURITY","PERFORMANCE"]}

{"record_id":"D35-B069-R005","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Batch Processing Boundary","subtopic":"Batch Verification","concept":"Batch verification reconciles selected input count, item outcomes, checkpoints, and final state to prove processing completeness.","knowledge_type":"VERIFICATION","question":"How should a batch processor be verified?","answer":"Verify that every selected item has an explicit outcome, successful effects satisfy their contracts, failed items are recoverable, and checkpoint state is consistent with actual progress.","explanation":"A process exiting successfully does not prove batch completeness. Verification requires accounting for every item and recovery boundary.","principle":"Batch correctness requires conservation of item identity across processing.","objective":"Verify batch completeness and recovery behavior.","requirements":["Input/output reconciliation","Outcome coverage","Checkpoint tests","Failure recovery"],"constraints":["Do not treat aggregate success as item completeness","Do not claim exactly-once processing without evidence"],"preconditions":["Batch selection and outcome contracts are defined"],"input":"Controlled batch test corpus.","output":"Completeness and recovery evidence.","expected_behavior":"Input items map to exactly one defined outcome under the declared processing semantics.","incorrect_code":"assert result.status == "SUCCESS"","corrected_code":"assert result.selected_count == result.success_count + result.failed_count + result.retryable_count + result.skipped_count\nassert result.unresolved_count == 0","failure_mode":"Aggregate result reports success while item accounting is incomplete.","expected_error":"BatchVerificationError.","cause":"Verification lacks item-level reconciliation.","root_cause":"Completion criteria are too weak.","solution":"Verify conservation of selected item identities and required outcomes.","edge_case":"Input source changes during processing; verification must use the declared snapshot semantics.","security_implication":"Verification must ensure no cross-tenant item contamination occurred.","performance_implication":"Full reconciliation can require additional reads; critical batches should retain sufficient evidence for verification.","test_case":"Run a batch with successful, failed, skipped, and retried items and compare final accounting.","test_input":"Mixed-outcome corpus.","expected_test_result":"All selected item IDs are accounted for according to the contract.","testing_guidance":"Include crash/restart and duplicate-processing scenarios.","verification_method":"Executed integration and recovery tests.","verification_guidance":"Verify actual counts and identities, not only aggregate status.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":null,"framework_version":null,"version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":["Python runtime and durable batch store"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B069-R001","D35-B069-R003","D35-B069-R004"],"depends_on":["D35-B069-R001"],"requires":["Batch verification corpus"],"extends":null,"refines":null,"specializes":null,"contrasts_with":null,"contradicts":null,"supersedes":null,"implements":null,"tests":"Batch processor","verifies":"Batch completeness and recovery","derived_from":["Batch verification and reconciliation practices"],"provenance":"Verification methodology is established; no execution performed for this record.","created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19","code_applicability":"CODE_RELEVANT","implementation_coverage":["TEST","VERIFICATION","EDGE-CASE","SECURITY","PERFORMANCE"]}

{"record_id":"D35-B070-R001","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Data Pipeline / Processing Boundary","subtopic":"Pipeline Stage Contract","concept":"A pipeline stage transforms an explicitly defined input contract into an output contract while exposing failure and resource semantics.","knowledge_type":"IMPLEMENTATION","question":"What should a data-pipeline stage contract contain?","answer":"Define input schema, output schema, transformation semantics, validation rules, error behavior, ordering requirements, and resource expectations.","explanation":"Explicit stage contracts allow stages to be independently tested and composed. A pipeline should not rely on undocumented assumptions about upstream data.","principle":"Every processing stage should have a verifiable boundary contract.","objective":"Implement composable data-processing stages.","requirements":["Input schema","Output schema","Transformation rules","Validation","Failure contract"],"constraints":["Do not silently coerce malformed data unless specified","Do not pass mutable shared state between stages without an explicit contract"],"preconditions":["Pipeline stages and data contracts are defined"],"input":"Stage input dataset or stream.","output":"Validated transformed dataset or stream.","expected_behavior":"The stage emits only outputs satisfying its declared contract or explicit failure records.","incorrect_code":"def transform(rows):\n    return [dict(r, total=r["qty"] * r["price"]) for r in rows]","corrected_code":"def transform(rows):\n    output = []\n    for row in rows:\n        if row["qty"] < 0 or row["price"] < 0:\n            raise ValueError("invalid row")\n        output.append({"id": row["id"], "total": row["qty"] * row["price"]})\n    return output","failure_mode":"Malformed input propagates silently and corrupts downstream processing.","expected_error":"StageValidationError or explicit rejected-record result.","cause":"Stage assumes upstream data is valid without enforcing its contract.","root_cause":"Input/output contracts are undocumented or unenforced.","solution":"Validate stage boundaries and define rejected-data semantics.","edge_case":"One malformed record appears in a large stream; stage policy must define whether processing stops or isolates the record.","security_implication":"Pipeline stages must enforce tenant/data-zone boundaries and prevent unauthorized data joins.","performance_implication":"Validation adds processing cost but can prevent expensive downstream failures.","test_case":"Pass valid and invalid records through the stage.","test_input":"Two valid and one invalid record.","expected_test_result":"Valid records produce contract-compliant output and invalid input follows the declared rejection policy.","testing_guidance":"Test schema boundaries, malformed records, empty input, and large values.","verification_method":"Contract tests and pipeline integration tests.","verification_guidance":"Verify downstream stages consume only declared output contracts.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":null,"framework_version":null,"version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":["Python runtime"],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.98,"related_records":["D35-B021-R001","D35-B022-R001","D35-B069-R001"],"depends_on":[],"requires":["Stage data contract"],"extends":null,"refines":null,"specializes":null,"contrasts_with":null,"contradicts":null,"supersedes":null,"implements":"Pipeline stage boundary","tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":["Data pipeline and contract-based architecture patterns"],"provenance":"Established data-processing pattern; code illustrative and not executed.","created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19","code_applicability":"CODE_RELEVANT","implementation_coverage":["CONCEPT","IMPLEMENTATION","EDGE-CASE","TEST","VERIFICATION","SECURITY","PERF