{"record_id":"D35-B079-R005","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Migration / Deployment Compatibility Implementation","subtopic":"Migration verification","concept":"Verify both structural completion and semantic correctness after migration.","knowledge_type":"verification","question":"What evidence is required before declaring a migration complete?","answer":"Verify migration execution state, schema structure, row or entity coverage, domain invariants, compatibility requirements, error counts, and application behavior against the migrated data.","explanation":"A migration can report completion while missing records, corrupting values, or violating application invariants.","principle":"Migration completion requires semantic verification, not merely script termination.","objective":"Establish evidence that migrated data satisfies the target contract.","requirements":["Migration accounting.","Invariant checks.","Compatibility checks.","Error/retry accounting."],"constraints":["Verification must account for intentionally excluded or transformed records.","Large datasets may require deterministic aggregate checks in addition to sampled records."],"preconditions":["Expected target invariants are defined."],"input":"Migrated dataset and migration metadata.","output":"Migration verification result.","expected_behavior":"Migration is accepted only when defined structural and semantic checks pass.","incorrect_code":"assert migration.exit_code == 0","corrected_code":"assert migration.completed\nassert verify_row_accounting()\nassert verify_target_schema()\nassert verify_domain_invariants()\nassert verify_compatibility()","failure_mode":"Successful process exit is treated as complete verification.","expected_error":"Silent data corruption or incomplete migration.","cause":"Verification scope is too narrow.","root_cause":"Execution completion conflated with semantic correctness.","solution":"Verify the resulting data and compatibility contract.","edge_case":"Expected transformations alter counts; verification must use transformation-aware accounting.","security_implication":"Verify permissions, ownership, and security-sensitive fields were not unintentionally changed.","performance_implication":"Full verification may be expensive; choose deterministic checks appropriate to data size and risk.","test_case":"Run migration against a controlled dataset containing normal, edge, and intentionally transformed records.","test_input":"Representative migration fixture.","expected_test_result":"All defined structural and semantic invariants pass.","testing_guidance":"Include rollback verification where rollback is supported.","verification_method":"Post-migration verification suite.","verification_guidance":"Do not mark migration VERIFIED solely because the migration process exited successfully.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.x","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.x","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":[],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"VERIFICATION_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B079-R001","D35-B079-R004","D35-B040-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B040-R001"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["D35-B079"],"tests":["D35-B079-R003","D35-B079-R004"],"verifies":["D35-B079-R001","D35-B079-R002","D35-B079-R003","D35-B079-R004"],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Martin Fowler, Evolutionary Database Design","Data migration verification principles"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}

{"record_id":"D35-B080-R001","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Runtime Configuration & Architecture Change Safety Implementation","subtopic":"Configuration change boundary","concept":"Treat runtime configuration changes as controlled architectural changes rather than arbitrary mutable state.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should runtime configuration changes be implemented safely?","answer":"Represent configuration as typed, validated state with explicit ownership, allowed ranges, change mechanisms, auditability, and clear application semantics for dynamic versus restart-required settings.","explanation":"Configuration can alter security, capacity, routing, feature availability, and data behavior. Treating it as untyped mutable data creates hidden architecture changes.","principle":"Configuration is executable policy and must have explicit contracts.","objective":"Prevent unsafe configuration changes from silently altering system behavior.","requirements":["Typed configuration schema.","Validation.","Change ownership.","Audit or change record.","Dynamic/static classification."],"constraints":["Not every setting should be mutable at runtime.","Secrets require separate protected handling.","Invalid configuration must not partially apply."],"preconditions":["Configuration ownership and lifecycle are defined."],"input":"Configuration change request.","output":"Validated applied configuration or rejected change.","expected_behavior":"Only valid and authorized configuration changes are applied according to their lifecycle semantics.","incorrect_code":"config[key] = value","corrected_code":"candidate = config.with_change(key, value)\nvalidate_config(candidate)\nauthorize_change(candidate)\napply_atomically(candidate)","failure_mode":"Arbitrary mutable configuration changes behavior immediately.","expected_error":"Invalid or unauthorized runtime behavior.","cause":"No schema, validation, or change boundary.","root_cause":"Configuration treated as ordinary dictionary state.","solution":"Introduce typed configuration and atomic change application.","edge_case":"One setting is valid individually but invalid in combination with another.","security_implication":"Configuration can disable security controls; sensitive changes require stronger authorization and audit.","performance_implication":"Dynamic configuration lookup can add overhead; snapshotting validated config avoids repeated parsing.","test_case":"Attempt a valid change, invalid value, unauthorized change, and incompatible combination.","test_input":"Four configuration change requests.","expected_test_result":"Only authorized compatible changes are applied.","testing_guidance":"Test schema validation, atomicity, rollback, audit, and concurrent change behavior.","verification_method":"Configuration contract and change-control tests.","verification_guidance":"Verify runtime consumers observe either the old complete configuration or the new complete configuration, not a partially applied state.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.x","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.x","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":[],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_CONFIGURATION_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B031-R001","D35-B029-R001","D35-B043-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B031-R001"],"requires":["D35-B043-R001"],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["D35-B080"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Microsoft Architecture Center, configuration management principles","OWASP Configuration and Secrets Management guidance"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B080-R002","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Runtime Configuration & Architecture Change Safety Implementation","subtopic":"Atomic configuration application","concept":"Apply related configuration changes as one validated snapshot.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"Why should related runtime configuration changes be applied atomically?","answer":"A configuration snapshot should be validated as a complete candidate and swapped as one unit so consumers cannot observe an internally inconsistent combination of settings.","explanation":"Applying fields individually can create transient states that violate architectural invariants.","principle":"Configuration consistency requires atomic snapshot replacement.","objective":"Prevent partial configuration states.","requirements":["Complete candidate configuration.","Cross-field validation.","Atomic publication."],"constraints":["Consumers should treat configuration snapshots as immutable.","Concurrent updates require conflict handling."],"preconditions":["Configuration can be represented as a complete snapshot."],"input":"Candidate configuration.","output":"Published immutable configuration snapshot.","expected_behavior":"Consumers observe a coherent configuration version.","incorrect_code":"config.timeout = new_timeout\nconfig.retries = new_retries","corrected_code":"candidate = Config(timeout=new_timeout, retries=new_retries)\nvalidate(candidate)\nconfig_store.publish(candidate)","failure_mode":"Consumers observe mixed old/new settings.","expected_error":"Inconsistent retry and timeout behavior.","cause":"Fields are updated independently.","root_cause":"No immutable configuration snapshot boundary.","solution":"Validate and publish a complete snapshot atomically.","edge_case":"A consumer caches an old snapshot during transition; semantics must define whether that is allowed.","security_implication":"Atomic publication prevents partial security-policy application.","performance_implication":"Immutable snapshots can reduce synchronization overhead for readers.","test_case":"Concurrently read configuration while applying a multi-field update.","test_input":"Old snapshot A and new snapshot B.","expected_test_result":"Readers observe either complete A or complete B according to publication semantics, never a mixed state.","testing_guidance":"Use concurrency tests and versioned snapshots.","verification_method":"Atomicity and concurrency tests.","verification_guidance":"Verify consumers do not mutate shared configuration snapshots.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.x","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.x","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":[],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ARCHITECTURAL_CONSISTENCY_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B031-R001","D35-B037-R001","D35-B080-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B031-R001"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["D35-B080"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Immutable configuration and atomic publication architectural principles"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B080-R003","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Runtime Configuration & Architecture Change Safety Implementation","subtopic":"Change blast-radius analysis","concept":"Evaluate the architectural blast radius of configuration changes before applying them.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How can configuration changes be prevented from unexpectedly affecting unrelated components?","answer":"Associate configuration keys with their consumers, invariants, resource effects, security implications, and restart requirements so a change can be evaluated before publication.","explanation":"A configuration field may be consumed by many modules and alter architecture-level behavior without source-code changes.","principle":"Change impact must follow dependency relationships, including configuration dependencies.","objective":"Make configuration-induced architecture changes discoverable and reviewable.","requirements":["Configuration-to-consumer mapping.","Impact metadata.","Change validation."],"constraints":["Consumer discovery must be maintained as architecture evolves.","Dynamic lookup can make static dependency discovery incomplete."],"preconditions":["Configuration keys have identifiable ownership and consumers."],"input":"Proposed configuration change.","output":"Impact analysis and change decision.","expected_behavior":"Affected components and relevant invariants are identified before application.","incorrect_code":"config['timeout'] = 0\nrestart_required = False","corrected_code":"impact = config_catalog.analyze_change('timeout', 0)\nvalidate_change_impact(impact)\napply_change_if_authorized(impact)","failure_mode":"Configuration change bypasses architecture review.","expected_error":"Unexpected dependency behavior or outage.","cause":"Configuration dependencies are invisible.","root_cause":"Architecture model excludes runtime configuration relationships.","solution":"Track configuration consumers and impact metadata.","edge_case":"A configuration key is used dynamically through plugins or reflection.","security_implication":"Security-control configuration changes should require explicit approval and audit.","performance_implication":"Impact analysis should be bounded and preferably precomputed for stable consumers.","test_case":"Change a timeout or concurrency setting and verify all declared consumers are included in the impact report.","test_input":"Configuration key with three registered consumers.","expected_test_result":"Impact analysis identifies all three consumers and relevant constraints.","testing_guidance":"Test missing consumer registration as an architecture regression.","verification_method":"Architecture metadata validation plus change tests.","verification_guidance":"Treat incomplete configuration dependency metadata as an architectural risk rather than assuming coverage.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.x","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.x","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":[],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ARCHITECTURE_GOVERNANCE_PATTERN","confidence":0.96,"related_records":["D35-B040-R001","D35-B031-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B040-R001","D35-B031-R001"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["D35-B080"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Architecture fitness function principles","Microsoft Architecture Center, configuration management"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B080-R004","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Runtime Configuration & Architecture Change Safety Implementation","subtopic":"Safe dynamic-change lifecycle","concept":"Use propose-validate-authorize-apply-verify semantics for high-impact runtime configuration changes.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"What lifecycle should a high-impact runtime configuration change follow?","answer":"A controlled change should be proposed, validated against configuration and architecture rules, authorized according to risk, applied atomically, observed, and verified against expected runtime behavior.","explanation":"High-impact settings can change security, capacity, routing, or correctness without a code deployment. A lifecycle prevents unreviewed changes from becoming invisible architecture modifications.","principle":"Runtime mutability requires governance proportional to impact.","objective":"Make high-impact configuration changes controlled and verifiable.","requirements":["Proposal representation.","Validation.","Authorization.","Atomic application.","Post-change verification."],"constraints":["Low-risk settings may use a lighter workflow.","Verification must distinguish configuration applied from intended behavior achieved."],"preconditions":["Configuration risk classes exist."],"input":"Proposed configuration change.","output":"Applied/rejected change plus verification evidence.","expected_behavior":"Only authorized valid changes are applied and their runtime effect is verified.","incorrect_code":"config.set('max_workers', 1000)","corrected_code":"proposal = propose_change('max_workers', 1000)\nvalidate(proposal)\nauthorize(proposal)\napply_atomically(proposal)\nverify_runtime_effect(proposal)","failure_mode":"High-impact configuration changes are applied without validation or verification.","expected_error":"Unexpected capacity, latency, or security behavior.","cause":"No change lifecycle.","root_cause":"Runtime configuration treated as an unrestricted control surface.","solution":"Implement risk-aware change governance.","edge_case":"Configuration applies successfully but dependency behavior does not change as expected.","security_implication":"Security-critical configuration changes should require stronger approval and immutable audit evidence.","performance_implication":"Post-change verification should avoid causing additional load that masks the actual configuration effect.","test_case":"Apply a high-impact configuration change in a controlled environment and verify both application and runtime effect.","test_input":"Controlled change to concurrency limit.","expected_test_result":"Change is validated, authorized, atomically applied, and its observed effect matches the intended policy.","testing_guidance":"Test rejection, partial application, concurrent proposal, rollback, and verification failure.","verification_method":"End-to-end configuration change lifecycle test.","verification_guidance":"Do not mark the change successful solely because the configuration store accepted it.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.x","framework":"","framework_version":"","version_range":"Python 3.x","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":[],"execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"GOVERNED_RUNTIME_CHANGE_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B080-R001","D35-B080-R002","D35-B040-R001","D35-B043-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B040-R001"],"requires":["D35-B043-R001"],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["D35-B080"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":["Google SRE change-management principles","Microsoft Architecture Center, operational configuration guidance"],"created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
