{"record_id":"D35-B092-R002","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Leader Election & Leadership Lease Implementation","subtopic":"Lease renewal","concept":"Leadership leases require periodic renewal and explicit expiry semantics.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should leadership renewal be implemented?","answer":"Renew a leadership lease before its expiry using bounded timing and relinquish leadership when renewal cannot be confirmed.","explanation":"A lease without reliable renewal can result in stale leaders continuing to act.","principle":"Leadership authority expires unless renewed by the authoritative coordinator.","objective":"Prevent stale leadership from persisting indefinitely.","requirements":["Lease expiry","Renewal deadline","Renewal confirmation"],"constraints":["Network delay","Clock differences","Coordinator failure"],"preconditions":["A lease was acquired"],"input":"Current lease and renewal context","output":"Renewed or expired leadership state","expected_behavior":"Failed renewal eventually causes leadership loss.","incorrect_code":"while leader:\n    do_work()","corrected_code":"while lease.active:\n    if not lease.renew():\n        break\n    do_work()","failure_mode":"Leader continues after lease expiry.","expected_error":"Expired authority used for leader-only operation.","cause":"Renewal failure ignored.","root_cause":"Lease validity is not checked during leadership lifecycle.","solution":"Require successful renewal and authoritative validity checks.","edge_case":"Renew response is delayed until after expiry.","security_implication":"Expired leases must never authorize privileged actions.","performance_implication":"Renewal interval must balance safety with coordination overhead.","test_case":"Force renewal failure and expiry.","test_input":"Valid lease followed by failed renewal.","expected_test_result":"Leadership becomes inactive.","testing_guidance":"Use a deterministic fake clock an