{"record_id":"D35-B092-R005","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Leader Election & Leadership Lease Implementation","subtopic":"Verification","concept":"Leader-election correctness requires concurrent acquisition, expiry, renewal, fencing, and recovery tests.","knowledge_type":"verification","question":"How should leader-election implementation be verified?","answer":"Test concurrent candidates, renewal, expiry, network partition, leadership loss, fencing, and re-election while asserting the documented authority invariants.","explanation":"Happy-path leader acquisition does not establish safety under distributed timing failures.","principle":"Leadership verification must target race conditions and stale authority.","objective":"Verify single-authority and safe-recovery invariants.","requirements":["Concurrency tests","Expiry tests","Fencing tests","Recovery tests"],"constraints":["Distributed timing must be controlled in tests"],"preconditions":["Leadership boundary exists"],"input":"Simulated cluster events","output":"Verified leadership outcomes","expected_behavior":"At most one valid authority exists under the coordination contract and stale authority is rejected where fencing is required.","incorrect_code":"assert acquire(node_a)\nassert acquire(node_b)","corrected_code":"assert acquire(node_a)\nassert not acquire(node_b)","failure_mode":"Tests accidentally accept multiple leaders.","expected_error":"Leadership invariant violated.","cause":"Incorrect test oracle.","root_cause":"Verification does not encode the actual authority invariant.","solution":"Define explicit safety and liveness properties.","edge_case":"Coordinator becomes unavailable during renewal.","security_implication":"Verification should include unauthorized leadership attempts.","performance_implication":"Stress tests can identify renewal contention and coordination load.","test_case":"Run election scenarios under controlled failures.","test_input":"Concurre