{"record_id":"D35-B095-R002","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Remote Procedure Call (RPC) Contract Implementation","subtopic":"Deadline propagation","concept":"RPC deadlines limit end-to-end waiting and should propagate through nested service calls.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should RPC deadlines be propagated?","answer":"Represent the remaining deadline explicitly and pass it to downstream calls without resetting it to a new full timeout.","explanation":"Independent per-hop timeouts can exceed the caller's intended latency budget.","principle":"Nested RPCs consume a shared end-to-end deadline budget.","objective":"Prevent unbounded downstream waiting.","requirements":["Deadline representation","Remaining-time calculation","Downstream propagation"],"constraints":["Clock and scheduling delays consume budget"],"preconditions":["Incoming request has a deadline or default budget"],"input":"Current deadline","output":"Remaining downstream budget","expected_behavior":"Downstream calls cannot extend the original deadline.","incorrect_code":"child.call(timeout=30)","corrected_code":"child.call(timeout=max(0, deadline.remaining()))","failure_mode":"Nested calls outlive the caller's budget.","expected_error":"Deadline budget exceeded.","cause":"Timeout reset at each hop.","root_cause":"No end-to-end deadline propagation.","solution":"Propagate remaining deadline.","edge_case":"Remaining budget is already zero.","security_implication":"Deadline propagation can reduce resource-exhaustion exposure.","performance_implication":"Deadline calculation is cheap but must avoid repeated unnecessary clock calls.","test_case":"Nest calls under a short deadline.","test_input":"Parent deadline shorter than child default timeout.","expected_test_result":"Child receives only remaining budget.","testing_guidance":"Use an injected clock.","verification_method":"Deterministic timeout tests.","verification_guidance":"Assert child timeout never exceeds parent remaining budget.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"gRPC","framework_version":"Version-specific","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":["grpcio"],"execution_requirements":"Compatible gRPC runtime","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B033-R004","D35-B047-R001","D35-B095-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B033-R004","D35-B095-R001"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["RPC deadline propagation"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":"gRPC deadline documentation; distributed timeout-budget principles","created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B095-R003","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Remote Procedure Call (RPC) Contract Implementation","subtopic":"Error mapping","concept":"RPC errors should distinguish transport failures, validation failures, authorization failures, and application failures.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should RPC errors be mapped?","answer":"Define a stable error taxonomy and map transport/provider errors into explicit application-level categories without losing diagnostic context.","explanation":"Clients need stable semantics while operators need enough context to diagnose the original failure.","principle":"Error translation preserves semantics while hiding infrastructure-specific implementation details.","objective":"Implement stable RPC failure semantics.","requirements":["Error taxonomy","Provider-to-domain mapping","Safe diagnostic metadata"],"constraints":["Do not leak sensitive infrastructure details"],"preconditions":["Error categories are defined"],"input":"Transport or application error","output":"Stable RPC error","expected_behavior":"Clients receive predictable error classes and operators retain traceable diagnostics.","incorrect_code":"except Exception:\n    raise RuntimeError('RPC failed')","corrected_code":"except TransportError as exc:\n    raise RpcUnavailable(str(exc)) from exc","failure_mode":"All failures become one ambiguous error.","expected_error":"Loss of actionable failure semantics.","cause":"Broad exception translation.","root_cause":"No explicit RPC error taxonomy.","solution":"Map errors by category and preserve cause chains internally.","edge_case":"Unknown provider exception.","security_implication":"Raw provider messages should not expose credentials, topology, or stack traces to untrusted clients.","performance_implication":"Error mapping should not perform expensive recovery work synchronously.","test_case":"Map representative RPC failure classes.","test_input":"Timeout