{"record_id":"D35-B096-R001","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Distributed Work Ownership / Claiming Implementation","subtopic":"Work claim contract","concept":"Distributed workers require an explicit claim operation that transfers ownership of a unit of work according to a defined concurrency rule.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should distributed work claiming be implemented?","answer":"Represent each work item with ownership state and use an atomic claim operation that succeeds for at most one eligible worker.","explanation":"Reading an unowned item and updating it later creates a race where multiple workers can perform the same work.","principle":"Work ownership must be established atomically.","objective":"Prevent concurrent workers from claiming the same unit of work.","requirements":["Work identity","Ownership state","Atomic claim","Claim timestamp or lease"],"constraints":["Workers can fail after claiming","Claims may need expiration"],"preconditions":["Work items have unique identity"],"input":"Work item and worker identity","output":"Claim result","expected_behavior":"Only one worker obtains the current claim.","incorrect_code":"if item.owner is None:\n    item.owner = worker","corrected_code":"if store.atomic_claim(item.id, worker):\n    process(item)","failure_mode":"Two workers observe unclaimed state and both process it.","expected_error":"Duplicate work execution.","cause":"Non-atomic read-modify-write.","root_cause":"Ownership acquisition lacks atomicity.","solution":"Use an atomic conditional claim.","edge_case":"Worker crashes immediately after claiming.","security_implication":"Only authorized workers may claim specific work classes.","performance_implication":"Claim contention should be bounded with efficient conditional updates.","test_case":"Race two workers against one item.","test_input":"Same work ID and two worker IDs.","expected_test_result":"Exactly one claim succeeds.","testing_guidance":"Run deterministic concurrency tests.","verification_method":"Atomicity tests.","verification_guidance":"Inspect ownership state after concurrent claims.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"None","framework_version":"N/A","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":"Persistent store supporting atomic conditional update","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B067-R001","D35-B087-R001","D35-B012-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B087-R001"],"requires":["Atomic persistence operation"],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["Distributed work claim boundary"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":"Distributed work-queue ownership patterns; database conditional-update principles","created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B096-R002","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Distributed Work Ownership / Claiming Implementation","subtopic":"Claim lease","concept":"A work claim may need a lease so ownership can recover after worker failure.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"When should a work claim use a lease?","answer":"Use a time-bounded claim lease when workers can fail and work must become reclaimable after a defined expiration policy.","explanation":"Permanent ownership can strand work indefinitely when the owner disappears.","principle":"Recoverable work ownership requires explicit expiration semantics.","objective":"Allow failed workers' work to be safely reclaimed.","requirements":["Lease expiry","Owner identity","Renewal policy","Reclaim rule"],"constraints":["Clock and timing assumptions","Worker may be slow rather than failed"],"preconditions":["Work can be safely retried or resumed"],"input":"Work claim and current time","output":"Active or reclaimable ownership","expected_behavior":"Expired claims become eligible according to policy without allowing overlapping valid ownership.","incorrect_code":"if claim.owner:\n    return False","corrected_code":"if claim.active(now):\n    return False\nreturn store.claim_if_expired(item_id, worker, now)","failure_mode":"Failed worker permanently owns work.","expected_error":"Stuck work item.","cause":"No claim expiry.","root_cause":"Ownership has no recovery semantics.","solution":"Add bounded claim lease and safe reclaim.","edge_case":"Original worker resumes after its lease expires.","security_implication":"Expired owners must lose authority to commit effects; fencing may be required.","performance_implication":"Lease renewal frequency affects database traffic.","test_case":"Expire a claim and reclaim it.","test_input":"Worker A claim expires, worker B attempts claim.","expected_test_result":"B can claim only after valid expiration conditions.","testing_guidance":"Test old owner committing after reclaim.","verification_method":"Lease and fencing integration tests.","verification_guidance":"Verify stale owner cannot create conflicting effects.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"None","framework_version":"N/A","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":"Persistent store with time-aware claim semantics","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B092-R003","D35-B096-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B096-R001"],"requires":["Fencing or equivalent stale-owner protection when necessary"],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["Recoverable work claim lease"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":"Lease-based work ownership patterns; distributed fencing principles","created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B096-R003","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Distributed Work Ownership / Claiming Implementation","subtopic":"Ownership heartbeat","concept":"Long-running work may renew ownership while processing, provided renewal does not incorrectly extend ownership after loss.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should long-running work renew its claim?","answer":"Renew claims before expiry using bounded deadlines and stop renewing after cancellation, authority loss, or unrecoverable errors.","explanation":"Renewal keeps legitimate long-running work owned while preserving recovery after worker failure.","principle":"Claim renewal extends authority only while the owner remains valid and active.","objective":"Support long-running distributed work safely.","requirements":["Renewal schedule","Lease validity","Cancellation handling"],"constraints":["Renewal failure can race with work completion"],"preconditions":["Work claim has renewable lease"],"input":"Claim and worker lifecycle","output":"Renewed or expired claim","expected_behavior":"Healthy owner renews; failed or cancelled owner eventually loses claim.","incorrect_code":"while processing:\n    claim.extend()","corrected_code":"while processing and not cancelled:\n    if not claim.renew(deadline):\n        stop_processing()\n        break","failure_mode":"Dead worker lease remains active or renewal continues after cancellation.","expected_error":"Stale ownership.","cause":"Renewal not coupled to worker lifecycle.","root_cause":"Lease and execution lifecycle are independent.","solution":"Tie renewal to valid processing state.","edge_case":"Renewal succeeds immediately before worker crashes.","security_implication":"Renewal must authenticate the current owner.","performance_implication":"Renewal intervals should be selected to balance recovery time and coordination cost.","test_case":"Fail renewal during processing.","test_input":"Long-running job with injected renewal failure.","expected_test_result":"Worker stops or follows documented safe policy.","testing_guidance":"Inject cancellation and renewal races.","verification_method":"Lifecycle/concurrency tests.","verification_guidance":"Verify claim expiry after renewal stops.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"None","framework_version":"N/A","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":"Lease-capable store","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ENGINEERING_PRACTICE","confidence":0.98,"related_records":["D35-B096-R002","D35-B092-R002"],"depends_on":["D35-B096-R002"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["Work-claim renewal"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":"Lease renewal and distributed work ownership principles","created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B096-R004","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Distributed Work Ownership / Claiming Implementation","subtopic":"Claim completion","concept":"Completion should be accepted only from the current valid owner and should transition the work item atomically where necessary.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should claimed work be completed safely?","answer":"Validate current ownership before committing completion and atomically transition the work state so stale owners cannot mark reclaimed work complete.","explanation":"Ownership can change while a worker is processing, making an unconditional completion update unsafe.","principle":"Completion authority must be tied to current ownership.","objective":"Prevent stale workers from completing work they no longer own.","requirements":["Owner validation","Atomic completion","Completion identity"],"constraints":["Worker can finish after lease expiry","Completion may need idempotency"],"preconditions":["Work item has ownership state"],"input":"Work ID, owner identity, claim generation","output":"Completed or rejected transition","expected_behavior":"Only current valid owner can complete the claim.","incorrect_code":"store.mark_done(item_id)","corrected_code":"store.complete_if_owner(item_id, worker_id, claim_generation)","failure_mode":"Old worker marks reclaimed work complete.","expected_error":"Stale completion accepted.","cause":"Completion lacks owner check.","root_cause":"Work ownership not enforced at completion boundary.","solution":"Use conditional completion with owner/generation validation.","edge_case":"Work completed exactly as claim expires.","security_implication":"Completion authorization must be enforced server-side.","performance_implication":"Conditional completion should be a single atomic operation where supported.","test_case":"Reclaim work then attempt stale completion.","test_input":"Old and new worker claims.","expected_test_result":"Old completion rejected; current completion accepted.","testing_guidance":"Test completion/expiry race.","verification_method":"Atomic conditional-update tests.","verification_guidance":"Inspect final state and completion actor.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"None","framework_version":"N/A","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":"Atomic persistent store","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B096-R002","D35-B096-R003","D35-B087-R002"],"depends_on":["D35-B096-R002"],"requires":["Atomic conditional update"],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["Safe distributed work completion"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":"Distributed work ownership and fencing principles","created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
