{"record_id":"D35-B097-R003","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Checkpoint / Resume State Implementation","subtopic":"Resume compatibility","concept":"Resume must validate that a checkpoint is compatible with the current executable, workflow, input, and state schema.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"What must be checked before resuming from a checkpoint?","answer":"Validate checkpoint schema, workflow version, input identity, integrity, and any required execution preconditions before resuming.","explanation":"A syntactically valid checkpoint can still be semantically incompatible with the current implementation.","principle":"Resume is conditional on compatibility, not merely checkpoint existence.","objective":"Prevent unsafe resume from obsolete state.","requirements":["Schema validation","Version compatibility","Input identity","Integrity validation"],"constraints":["Some workflows intentionally support migration"],"preconditions":["Checkpoint exists"],"input":"Checkpoint and current runtime metadata","output":"Resume decision","expected_behavior":"Only compatible checkpoints are resumed.","incorrect_code":"if checkpoint:\n    resume(checkpoint)","corrected_code":"if compatible(checkpoint, runtime):\n    resume(checkpoint)\nelse:\n    recover_or_restart()","failure_mode":"Old checkpoint drives incompatible code.","expected_error":"Resume compatibility failure.","cause":"Existence used as compatibility proof.","root_cause":"Resume contract lacks validation.","solution":"Validate all compatibility dimensions.","edge_case":"Checkpoint can be migrated by an explicit migration handler.","security_implication":"Checkpoint integrity must be verified before loading potentially sensitive or executable data.","performance_implication":"Compatibility checks should be inexpensive compared with full recomputation.","test_case":"Attempt resume with old schema and changed input.","test_input":"Compatible and incompatible checkpoints.","expected_test_result":"Only compatible state resumes.","testing_guidance":"Test explicit migration separately from direct resume.","verification_method":"Resume compatibility tests.","verification_guidance":"Record exact rejection reason.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"None","framework_version":"N/A","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":"Checkpoint and runtime metadata","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_PATTERN","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B045-R001","D35-B097-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B097-R001"],"requires":[],"extends":[],"refines":["D35-B045-R001"],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["Resume compatibility boundary"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":"Durable workflow recovery and schema compatibility principles","created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B097-R004","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Checkpoint / Resume State Implementation","subtopic":"Exactly-once resume semantics","concept":"Resume logic must avoid duplicating non-idempotent effects when the checkpoint position does not perfectly align with external side effects.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How can resume avoid duplicate external effects?","answer":"Place checkpoints at safe boundaries, make effects idempotent where possible, or persist effect completion and checkpoint advancement under a coordinated transaction.","explanation":"A crash between an external effect and checkpoint persistence creates ambiguity about whether the effect already occurred.","principle":"Checkpoint position alone does not prove external side-effect completion.","objective":"Implement safe resume semantics around side effects.","requirements":["Safe checkpoint boundaries","Idempotency or effect records","Explicit recovery policy"],"constraints":["Exactly-once external effects are not generally guaranteed by a local checkpoint alone"],"preconditions":["Workflow performs external effects"],"input":"Work state and effect state","output":"Safe resume decision","expected_behavior":"Recovery cannot blindly repeat uncertain non-idempotent effects.","incorrect_code":"perform_effect()\nsave_checkpoint()","corrected_code":"effect_id = stable_id(work, step)\nperform_idempotent_effect(effect_id)\nsave_checkpoint()","failure_mode":"Crash causes duplicate external action.","expected_error":"Duplicate external effect.","cause":"Effect and checkpoint are separate durable operations.","root_cause":"Recovery protocol ignores uncertainty window.","solution":"Use idempotency, durable effect state, or transactional coordination.","edge_case":"External provider completed effect but local process crashed before recording success.","security_implication":"Repeated privileged effects can be dangerous and require strong idempotency controls.","performance_implication":"Durable effect tracking adds storage overhead.","test_case":"Inject crash between effect and checkpoint.","test_input":"Effect succeeds then checkpoint fails.","expected_test_result":"Recovery follows documented idempotency/reconciliation semantics.","testing_guidance":"Do not label local checkpointing as exactly-once external execution without evidence.","verification_method":"Fault-injection integration tests.","verification_guidance":"Verify effect count and recovery decision.","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","framework":"None","framework_version":"N/A","version_range":"Python 3.11+","dependencies":[],"execution_requirements":"Controlled external-effect test double","execution_status":"NOT_EXECUTED","validation_status":"ILLUSTRATIVE","evidence_level":"ESTABLISHED_DISTRIBUTED_SYSTEMS_PRINCIPLE","confidence":0.99,"related_records":["D35-B012-R001","D35-B017-R001","D35-B097-R001"],"depends_on":["D35-B097-R001"],"requires":["Idempotent effect or durable effect record"],"extends":[],"refines":[],"specializes":[],"contrasts_with":[],"contradicts":[],"supersedes":[],"implements":["Safe checkpoint/effect boundary"],"tests":[],"verifies":[],"derived_from":[],"provenance":"Distributed transaction and checkpoint/recovery principles","created_at":"2026-09-19","updated_at":"2026-09-19"}
{"record_id":"D35-B097-R005","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Checkpoint / Resume State Implementation","subtopic":"Checkpoint verification","concept":"Checkpoint systems require crash, corruption, compatibility, resume, and duplicate-effect verification.","knowledge_type":"verification","question":"How should checkpoint and resume implementation be verified?","answer":"Test crash points, corrupted checkpoints, incompatible versions, successful resume, repeated resume, and uncertain external effects.","explanation":"The value of checkpointing is determined by recovery correctness under failure, not by successful checkpoint creation alone.","principle":"Recovery verification must exercise failure windows explicitly.","objective":"Verify safe and deterministic resume behavior.","requirements":["Crash tests","Corruption tests","Compatibility tests","Effect-duplication tests"],"constraints":["Fault injection should be deterministic"],"preconditions":["Checkpoint mechanism exists"],"input":"Failure and recovery scenarios","output":"Resume verification results","expected_behavior":"Recovery resumes only compatible state and does not introduce unintended duplicate effects.","incorrect_code":"assert resume(checkpoint)","corrected_code":"assert recovery_outcome(checkpoint, failure_trace) == expected","failure_mode":"Recovery path remains untested.","expected_error":"False confidence in resumability.","cause":"Only successful restart tested.","root_cause":"Failure windows omitted from verification.","solution":"Build a checkpoint failure matrix.","edge_case":"Repeated recovery from the same checkpoint.","security_implication":"Corrupt or unauthorized checkpoints must be rejected.","performance_implication":"Checkpoint frequency and recovery duration should be measured separately from correctness.","test_case":"Execute complete checkpoint/recovery matrix.","test_input":"Crash, corruption, version mismatch, effect uncertainty.","expecte