{"record_id":"D35-B098-R001","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Runtime Topology & Dependency Graph Implementation","subtopic":"Topology model","concept":"Runtime topology represents deployed components and their communication or dependency relationships independently from static source architecture.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should runtime topology be represented?","answer":"Model runtime nodes, component identities, endpoints, dependency edges, and observed state as explicit graph entities.","explanation":"Static architecture and runtime topology are related but not identical because deployment can vary by environment.","principle":"Runtime topology is observed operational state derived from deployed components and relationships.","objective":"Implement a queryable runtime topology boundary.","requirements":["Node identity","Relationship identity","Endpoint metadata","Observation state"],"constraints":["Topology changes dynamically","Observations can be incomplete"],"preconditions":["Runtime components expose identity and relationship metadata"],"input":"Runtime component observations","output":"Topology graph","expected_behavior":"Components and relationships can be added, updated, and removed without conflating observation with design intent.","incorrect_code":"topology = {'api': 'db'}","corrected_code":"topology.add_node(service_id)\ntopology.add_edge(service_id, dependency_id, relation='depends_on')","failure_mode":"Runtime relationships become unstructured strings.","expected_error":"Topology cannot support reliable queries.","cause":"No graph model.","root_cause":"Runtime topology represented as ad hoc metadata.","solution":"Use typed graph entities and edges.","edge_case":"A dependency is observed but its identity cannot be resolved.","security_implication":"Topology data may reveal sensitive infrastructure structure.","performance_implication":"Incremental graph updates avoid rebuilding the e