{"record_id":"D35-B098-R002","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Runtime Topology & Dependency Graph Implementation","subtopic":"Dependency graph construction","concept":"Runtime dependency edges should be created from evidence such as configuration, service discovery, communication metadata, or explicit registration rather than guessed solely from names.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should runtime dependency edges be established?","answer":"Create edges from authoritative or observable evidence and attach provenance and observation metadata to each relationship.","explanation":"A guessed dependency graph can produce incorrect operational decisions.","principle":"Runtime topology relationships should be evidence-backed.","objective":"Build trustworthy runtime dependency relationships.","requirements":["Relationship evidence","Source metadata","Observation timestamp"],"constraints":["Some dependencies may be indirect or dynamically discovered"],"preconditions":["Evidence source exists"],"input":"Dependency evidence","output":"Provenance-backed graph edge","expected_behavior":"Each runtime edge can be traced to its observation source.","incorrect_code":"if service_name.startswith('db'):\n    add_dependency(service, 'database')","corrected_code":"add_edge(service, dependency, evidence=observation.source, observed_at=observation.time)","failure_mode":"False dependency relationships drive operations.","expected_error":"Topology evidence mismatch.","cause":"Inference without provenance.","root_cause":"Graph construction treats guesses as facts.","solution":"Attach provenance and confidence to edges.","edge_case":"Conflicting evidence sources report different dependencies.","security_implication":"Topology evidence must respect access controls.","performance_implication":"Evidence metadata should be compact and indexed for graph queries.","test_case":"Build graph from conflicting observations.","test_input":"Mult