{"record_id":"D35-B098-R003","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"Runtime Topology & Dependency Graph Implementation","subtopic":"Topology change detection","concept":"Runtime topology changes should be detected by comparing versioned observations rather than rebuilding assumptions from scratch.","knowledge_type":"implementation","question":"How should runtime topology changes be detected?","answer":"Maintain a versioned observed topology and compute additions, removals, and relationship changes between observation snapshots or event streams.","explanation":"Explicit change detection enables targeted reconciliation and auditability.","principle":"Topology change is a first-class event derived from observed state differences.","objective":"Implement reliable runtime topology change detection.","requirements":["Versioned observations","Stable identities","Diff mechanism"],"constraints":["Observation snapshots may be incomplete"],"preconditions":["Two comparable topology observations exist"],"input":"Previous and current topology","output":"Topology change set","expected_behavior":"Only evidence-supported changes are emitted.","incorrect_code":"return current != previous","corrected_code":"return diff_topology(previous, current)","failure_mode":"All topology differences are treated as equivalent.","expected_error":"Loss of change semantics.","cause":"No typed diff.","root_cause":"Topology represented only as snapshots.","solution":"Emit typed node and edge changes.","edge_case":"Temporary observation loss appears as mass deletion.","security_implication":"Topology changes should be auditable when operationally sensitive.","performance_implication":"Graph diff complexity depends on node/edge count; stable IDs reduce unnecessary work.","test_case":"Compare topology snapshots with additions and removals.","test_input":"Previous and current graphs.","expected_test_result":"Typed change set is correct.","testing_guidance":"Test incomple