{"record_id":"D35-B100-R001","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"End-to-End Architecture Implementation Verification","subtopic":"Architecture-to-code traceability","concept":"Architecture implementation verification establishes traceability from architectural components and contracts to concrete modules, interfaces, adapters, tests, and deployment boundaries.","knowledge_type":"verification","question":"How can architecture-to-code traceability be verified?","answer":"Map each architectural component and contract to implementation artifacts and corresponding verification evidence, then identify unmapped or contradictory elements.","explanation":"Architecture is not implemented merely because code exists; each important architectural responsibility needs an identifiable implementation boundary.","principle":"Every required architectural responsibility should have traceable implementation and verification evidence.","objective":"Verify architecture-to-implementation completeness.","requirements":["Architecture inventory","Implementation mapping","Contract mapping","Test mapping"],"constraints":["Some architecture elements are intentionally conceptual","Mappings require version awareness"],"preconditions":["Architecture and implementation inventories exist"],"input":"Architecture model and code inventory","output":"Traceability matrix","expected_behavior":"Required architecture elements map to concrete implementation artifacts or are explicitly marked not implemented.","incorrect_code":"assert len(files) > 0","corrected_code":"assert all(component in traceability for component in required_components)","failure_mode":"Code volume is mistaken for architecture coverage.","expected_error":"Unmapped architectural responsibility.","cause":"No traceability model.","root_cause":"Implementation presence confused with implementation completeness.","solution":"Build component-to-code-to-test traceability.","edge_case":"One implementation co