{"record_id":"D35-B100-R004","dataset_id":"D35","dataset_version":"1.0","schema_version":"1.0","topic":"End-to-End Architecture Implementation Verification","subtopic":"Runtime architecture verification","concept":"Static architecture verification must be complemented by runtime checks for wiring, dependency availability, boundary behavior, and operational invariants.","knowledge_type":"verification","question":"Why is static architecture verification insufficient?","answer":"Static checks can establish structural relationships but cannot prove runtime dependency wiring, lifecycle behavior, availability, or dynamic configuration correctness.","explanation":"A correctly structured codebase can still fail because composition, environment, transport, or runtime state is incorrect.","principle":"Architecture verification requires both structural and runtime evidence.","objective":"Verify that implemented architecture works as assembled.","requirements":["Static checks","Runtime checks","Dependency health checks","Integration scenarios"],"constraints":["Runtime verification depends on environment fidelity"],"preconditions":["Application can be assembled in an isolated test environment"],"input":"Built application and runtime scenarios","output":"Runtime architecture evidence","expected_behavior":"Required components initialize, communicate, fail, and recover according to architecture contracts.","incorrect_code":"assert imports_succeed()","corrected_code":"assert system.start() == READY\nassert system.verify_dependencies() == []","failure_mode":"Import success is treated as runtime architecture success.","expected_error":"Wiring or lifecycle defect remains hidden.","cause":"Only static validation performed.","root_cause":"Runtime behavior not included in architecture verification.","solution":"Add controlled runtime integration verification.","edge_case":"Optional dependency unavailable while core service remains operational.","security_implication":"Runtime tests must v